\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen robust, dollar survives stock declines. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Daniel Sternoff \par \uc2 750 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 23:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, March 13 (Reuters) - The yen rallied to six-week peaks against the dollar and neared an all-time high against the euro on Monday as traders bet Japan was poised to emerge from a technical recession at the end of 1999. \par \par \uc2  Falling U.S. stock prices also took a toll on the dollar, which slipped marginally against Europe's single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dodged even steeper losses as Wall Street stemmed an early tide of severe selling pressure. \par \par \uc2  The yen muscled higher as the market shrugged off worse than expected data overnight showing Japan's gross domestic product, the broadest measure of economic growth, contracted 1.4 percent from October to November. \par \par \uc2  Dealers had been well prepared for a gloomy report, and chose instead to zero in on underlying components pointing to a brighter future for Japan, such as an unexpected spike in corporate capital spending. \par \par \uc2  "The yen's gains are a carry-over from the GDP breakdown which showed capex numbers were better in Japan, suggesting the outward looking economic potential is better," said Mike Malpede, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at the Refco Group. \par \par \uc2  The dollar slid as low as 104.81 yen in early New York trading, its lowest level since January 28, before regaining its poise as U.S. stock markets trimmed morning losses. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar bounced back to close at 105.61 yen\tab  , a loss of 0.58 percent from its Friday close.\par The yen climbed nearly 0.40 percent against the euro\tab      to close at 101.87 yen, just under one yen above its record low of 100.90 hit last week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Malpede said he believed the Japanese economy could grow as much as 1 percent this year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "It's not robust, but it's better than recession," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers expect Japan's Economic Planning Agency will upgrade its growth forecasts in a monthly report due Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The yen has also received a shot in the arm this month as Japanese investors bring funds back home to adjust their books before the current fiscal year ends on March 31.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's gains were limited by fears that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may yet again \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to halt the yen's rapid appreciation.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par EURO PULLED OFF HIGHS AS U.S. STOCKS TRIM LOSSES\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro\tab   gained 0.18 percent on the dollar, closing at 96.45 cents, after earlier rising to an 11-day high of 97.28 cents as the dollar was infected by fears a global decline in technology stocks would hurt the U.S. Nasdaq index.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "It's clear the equity market is not as depressed as people thought it would be," said Doug Carp, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trader at Manufacturers and Traders Bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Nasdaq closed 2.80 percent weaker after bouncing back from losses of more than 4 percent in morning trading. The blue-chip Dow Jones industrial average eked out slim gains of 0.18 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Chris Widness, senior international economist with Chase Securities in New York, said the bounce back by stocks had been good for the dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "But going forward I think it's still going to be a rough week for the dollar because we have a whole slew of economic numbers that could suggest the (Federal Reserve) has a lot to do," Widness said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par February retail sales are released on Tuesday, the Producer Price Index (PPI) on Thursday and the Consumer Price Index (CPI) on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((U.S. Financial Markets Desk, 21 2859 1690)).\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 2204GMT.  All data taken from Reuters\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2130GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab    US Close US Close  %Chg   YTD %  1999 Cls\par \tab \tab \tab    13 Mar.  10 Mar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/dlr\tab \tab    0.9645   0.9628   +0.18   -4.39   1.0070\par Dlr/yen\tab \tab     105.61   106.23   -0.58   +3.93   102.21\par Euro/yen\tab \tab    101.87   102.24   -0.36   -0.83   103.10\par Dlr/swiss\tab \tab   1.6700   1.6710   -0.06   +5.08   1.5902\par Stg/dlr\tab \tab     1.5792   1.5759   +0.21   -2.58   1.6176\par Dlr/can\tab \tab     1.4608   1.4576   +0.22   +0.84   1.4455\par Aus/dlr\tab \tab     0.6162   0.6146   +0.26   -6.35   0.6563\par Euro/swiss\tab \tab  1.6105   1.6085   +0.12   +0.31   1.6036\par Euro/stg\tab \tab    0.6110   0.6104   +0.10   -2.16   0.6239.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw3d04lue\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
