\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen edges higher ahead of Japan growth report. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Daniel Sternoff \par \uc2 681 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 23:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, March 10 (Reuters) - The yen rose against the dollar and euro on Friday despite the threat the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt its climb, as dealers positioned for a key Japanese economic growth report next week. \par \par \uc2  Europe's single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , meanwhile, gave up this week's hard-fought gains against the dollar, dragged lower as it slumped back toward lifetime lows against the yen. \par \par \uc2  Japan on Monday releases gross domestic product data (GDP) for its October-December quarter. \par \par \uc2  Expectations the report will show Japan posted a second consecutive quarterly decline - technically a recession - pushed the yen to six-month lows against the dollar just over two weeks ago. \par \par \uc2  But the yen has since rebounded a sharp 5 percent against the dollar as forward-looking data have raised optimism about Japan's prospects. \par \par \uc2  "I think the feeling now among Japanese banks is that the numbers will be better than expected," said Wing Tso, dealer as Sanwa Bank in New York. \par \par \uc2  "Customers sold dollar/yen, thinking the yen will strengthen off of this number," he said. \par \par \uc2  The yen was also bolstered by an upbeat economic assessment by the Bank of Japan in its monthly report, which said Japan's economy had recently started to improve, noting an improvement in capital spending, corporate sentiment and profits. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar slipped 0.35 percent against the yen to close at 106.23 yen \tab from 106.60 on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro fell 0.80 percent to 102.24 yen, little more than a yen above its 100.90 yen all-time low hit on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The yen's rapid gains this week prompted the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market, selling its own \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , because officials fear a rising yen could choke off recovery.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I think there is a speculative attack on euro/yen right now, and they are going to try and get a reaction out of the BOJ," said Dennis Heidt, chief dealer at Banque Paribas.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Sanwa's Tso said that while Monday's growth report could push the yen higher, fears the Bank of Japan would step in would limit its gains to around the 105 per dollar level.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Against the dollar, the euro weakened 0.35 percent to 96.28 cents  96.62 cents on Thursday, in a day of lackluster trading with little for the market to focus on.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said the euro's movements mirrored a recent pattern where better European economic data hoisted the euro only a short way before investors again lost confidence and sold the unit off.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On Thursday, speculation had begun to mount that Europe's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would soon boost interest rates again to subdue rising inflationary pressures which appeared compounded by the euro's recent sharp decline.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But worries the Europeans may still be behind the tightening curve has sent enough shudders through the market to keep the euro from staking out more gains.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In fact, many analysts expect the euro to remain under pressure for some time, with some even calling for more record lows, taking out the 93.90 life low made recently.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 2156GMT.  All data taken from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Reuterswith percent change calculated from the daily U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par close at 2130GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab    US Close US Close  %Chg   YTD %  1999\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Cls\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab    10 Mar.  09 Mar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/dlr\tab \tab    0.9628   0.9662   -0.35   -4.05   1.0070\par Dlr/yen\tab \tab     106.23   106.60   -0.35   +4.30   102.21\par Euro/yen\tab \tab    102.24   103.06   -0.80   -0.04   103.10\par Dlr/swiss\tab \tab   1.6710   1.6628   +0.49   +4.57   1.5902\par Stg/dlr\tab \tab     1.5759   1.5812   -0.34   -2.25   1.6176\par Dlr/can\tab \tab     1.4576   1.4565   +0.08   +0.76   1.4455\par Aus/dlr\tab \tab     0.6146   0.6155   -0.15   -6.22   0.6563\par Euro/swiss\tab \tab  1.6085   1.6072   +0.08   +0.22   1.6036\par Euro/stg\tab \tab    0.6104   0.6107   -0.05   -2.12   0.6239.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw3a04wpb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
