\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr Down Vs Yen; Market Rethinks Japan 4th Quarter GDP \b0\par\par\uc2  By Arran Scott \par \uc2 708 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 06:33\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The dollar edged lower against the yen Friday in Tokyo, as traders adjusted positions on speculation that Japan's economy didn't perform as badly late last year as previously thought. \par \par \uc2  The downside, however, was firmly supported by fears that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets once again in order to stem the yen's rise. \par \par \uc2  Mixed signals out of Japan have often sent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on a wild goose chase. This week was no exception. \par \par \uc2  Market players had expected that Japan's economy took a sharp nosedive in the fourth quarter of 1999. Analysts had estimated on average that gross domestic product due out Monday morning would show the economy contracted by 1.2% from the previous quarter. \par \par \uc2  However, data released Thursday sent many analysts scrambling over the last twenty four hours to revise upward their GDP estimates. Critically, a finance ministry survey suggested that business investment wasn't as weak as originally expected. Moreover, machinery orders data, a leading indictor of such investment, indicated the outlook for investment seemed bright. \par \par \uc2  Economists now estimate on average that the economy contracted by only 0.9% from the previous quarter. \par \par \uc2  "At the beginning, many people said GDP contracted by 1.8% or 1.9%. But yesterday we saw some good economic statistics and now some people say the figures will be boosted," said Kazuteru Hasegawa, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Bank of America in Tokyo. "This supported the yen." \par \par \uc2  Nevertheless, with the BOJ lurking in the shadows, traders were reluctant to get short on dollars, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "There is strong fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  so we can't sell the dollar aggressively. But we can't really buy the dollar either, on the off chance that the GDP data is stronger than expected," said a Japanese city bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT (12:15 a.m. EST), the dollar was quoted at Y106.35, below Y106.59 late Thursday in New York. The dollar was at Y106.85 late Thursday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $0.9673, higher than $0.9666 late Thursday in New York. The euro was at $0.9623 in Tokyo Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Market players generally believe that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  will do what it takes - through the Bank of Japan - to prevent the yen from appreciating before the fiscal year ends on March 31. \par \par \uc2  Bank of America's Hasegawa said he thinks MOF has drawn the line at Y105. \par \par \uc2  "I think they will try to hold the dollar's value above Y105," he said. \par \par \uc2  For now, initial support for the dollar lies between Y106.10-Y106.20, ahead of firm support around Y105.75, other dealers said. \par \par \uc2  While concerns about possible BOJ action support the dollar's downside, dealers said the upside is also limited. \par \par \uc2  The market is still slightly long on the dollar against the yen, Hasegawa said. Therefore, "whenever the dollar comes up to the Y107 level, we see selling by Japanese and European speculators and investors," he said. \par \par \uc2  As a result dealers said they expect the dollar to stick to narrow ranges centered around the mid-Y106 level for the rest of the Asian session. \par \par \uc2  In other trading, the euro traced the dollar's moves against the yen. Traders said that Japanese investors are still eager to sell the euro around mid-Y103. However, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears are supporting the downside. Initial support is expected around Y102.50, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y102.87, down from Y103.03 in New York late Thursday. The euro was at Y102.82 in Tokyo late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.5833, up from $1.5814 in New York late Thursday. Sterling was at $1.5805 in Tokyo late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  -By Arran Scott; 813-5255-2929; arran.scott@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates which accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture which is updated hourly. \par \par \uc2  Subscribers can find this table: \par \par \uc2  -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087. \par \par \uc2  -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX \par \par \uc2  -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT \par \par \uc2  -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw3a01axl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
