\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen gains despite fears of more BoJ moves. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Svea Herbst-Bayliss \par \uc2 818 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 15:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, March 9 (Reuters) - The yen climbed against the dollar and euro on Thursday, boosted by stronger than expected economic data and Japanese investors' efforts to bring funds home before their fiscal year ends at the end of March. \par \par \uc2  Holding gains of more than half a percent against the dollar and euro as New York trading got under way, the yen appears to have shaken off the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's efforts to slow the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent sharp gains. \par \par \uc2  Yet lingering nervousness the Bank of Japan may be planning another assault has narrowed the day's trading range so far and may keep the dollar and euro from slipping through important support levels. \par \par \uc2  "The probability of more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  today seems low, but you can never rule it out especially if stops should be hit," said Mellon Bank strategist Marc Chandler in New York. \par \par \uc2  Overnight the yen received a boost when Japan's core private sector machinery orders, excluding orders for machinery at electric power companies and for ships, rose 0.8 percent in January, far exceeding analysts' calls for a 7.7 percent drop. Also news that Japanese firms' capital spending dipped by less than expected between October and December helped. \par \par \uc2  This helps reinforce the notion Japan's economy may soon turn the corner even though analysts forecast Japan's gross domestic product data, expected on Monday, will show a sharp decline in the fourth quarter of last year, sending the nation back into recession. \par \par \uc2  Also "the yen has been helped pretty much by the flows story, that is based on good gains in the Nikkei, and also the repatriation story which is a seasonal factor," said Mike Moran, treasury economist at Standard Chartered in London. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yen had now trimmed most of its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  induced losses and may head toward critical levels at 105.80 yen to the dollar and 102 yen to the euro. \par \par \uc2  But Japan's Vice Finance Minister Nobuaki Usui said that volatile movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market were undesirable and that more action would be taken if necessary. He also confused the market by saying \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  during overseas trading on Wednesday, declining however to say what \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  they bought for yen. \par \par \uc2  Officials confirmed Wednesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the second such action the bank took this year. \par \par \uc2  "There is the possibility of follow-up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but honestly it is very hard to tell what may happen today," said Refco Group senior analyst Mike Malpede. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile the euro inched more than a quarter of a percent higher against the dollar which allowed it to trade more than a full cent above Wednesday's one-week low of $0.9519. It took comfort in better economic data and more hawkish comments from European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  vice president Christian Noyer said euro zone growth in 2000 and 2001 could be higher than three percent and that inflation would be below two percent in the same period. \par \par \uc2  And the bank's chief economist Otmar Issing told a German newspaper that the bank was in a tightening trend in light of accelerating growth rates and rising inflation risks. \par \par \uc2  "I think the speculation about an interest rate hike next week could start to mount because the comments are more hawkish and oil prices are still high and pose inflationary risks," Chandler said. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was little changed across the board after the Bank of England left its key repo rate unchanged at 6.0 percent, meeting analysts' expectations. \par \par \uc2      ((--Svea Herbst-Bayliss, U.S. Financial Markets Desk, \par \par \uc2  212-859-1639 )) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 9:39 a.m. (1439 GMT). All data taken from \par \par \uc2  Reuters with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close \par \par \uc2  at 4:30 p.m. (2130 GMT). \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab    Last     US Close  %Chg   YTD %     1999\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab March 8\tab \tab \tab  Close\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/dlr\tab \tab    0.9635   0.9605   +0.31   -4.32   1.0070\par Dlr/yen\tab \tab     106.31   107.21   -0.84   +4.01   102.21\par Euro/yen\tab \tab    102.36   102.98   -0.60   -0.72   103.10\par Dlr/swiss\tab \tab   1.6670   1.6716   -0.28   +4.83   1.5902\par Stg/dlr\tab \tab     1.5793   1.5803   -0.06   -2.37   1.6176\par Can/dlr\tab \tab     1.4562   1.4561   +0.01   +0.74   1.4455\par Aus/dlr\tab \tab     0.6133   0.6086   +0.77   -6.55   0.6563\par Euro/swiss\tab \tab  1.6060   1.6062   -0.01   +0.15   1.6036\par Euro/stg\tab \tab    0.6097   0.6073   +0.40   -2.28   0.6239\par  All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news ...\tab     Debt...   Indicators...\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports..\tab \tab \tab \tab \par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \par \par All spots\tab \pa