\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar yields to euro and yen in U.S. trade. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Daniel Sternoff \par \uc2 639 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 23:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      NEW YORK, March 9 (Reuters) - The dollar drooped across the \par \par \uc2  board on Thursday as the euro rebounded from recent heavy \par \par \uc2  selling and the yen found support from stronger than expected \par \par \uc2  Japanese data and capital inflows ahead of the fiscal year-end. \par \par \uc2  The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bounced to its highest level against \par \par \uc2  the dollar in a week and stabilised around two yen above its \par \par \uc2  all-time floor against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit on Tuesday, \par \par \uc2  but dealers doubted the euro could sustain its gains. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro\tab   gained nearly a cent on the day, pushing as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par high as 97 cents in New York hours before slipping back to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par close at 96.62 cents.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "If you asked me yesterday what would surprise me, I'd say\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par having the euro go up," said Peter Lorraine, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  manager at Brown Brothers Harriman in New York.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The euro slumped to a week low on Wednesday, dangling just\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1-1/2 cents from a record floor at one point.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Lorraine attributed the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rise to a few large euro\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par orders in the morning, which forced some players who had been\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par betting the euro would remain under pressure to adjust their\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par positions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro also found support from news that growth in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 11-nation euro zone rose 0.9 percent in the fourth quarter and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par by hawkish comments on from European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Vice\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par President Christian Noyer.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Q4 pan-European data was seen by the market as being euro\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bullish," said Paul Podolsky, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FleetBoston.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But most analysts said the euro was vulnerable to return to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par record lows.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "The euro is in a structural downtrend against the dollar,"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said Kenneth Bercuson, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at Donaldson, Lufkin\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and Jenrette.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Bercuson said soaring U.S. growth and productivity and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par higher rates of return would keep the dollar well supported.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Only aggressive Federal Reserve rate hikes which prompt sharp\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par declines on Wall Street would hit the dollar, he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar meanwhile dropped more than 0.5 percent against\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the yen in the wake of news that Japan's core private sector\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par machinery orders rose 0.8 percent in January, far outstripping\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par analysts' calls for a 7.7 percent drop.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts also cited the repatriation of Japanese funds held\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par overseas ahead of the end of the fiscal year this month as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par another factor buoying the yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par New York traders pushed the dollar as low as 106.19 yen,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par despite the threat the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the yen as it did in Asian hours on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts said the BoJ's solo action with no coordination\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with U.S. or European central banks had emboldened some\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par speculators.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The BoJ is alone on this and the market knows that,"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Podolsky said. "It would be entirely different if they'd\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  with the ECB or with someone else. That tempts the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market to test them."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But caution prevailed, and the dollar rebounded to close at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 106.60\tab  , or 0.57 percent weaker than its 107.21 close on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts are already bracing for a soft fourth quarter\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par gross domestic product report due out of Japan on Monday. Such\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a report would technically put Japan back into recession and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par analysts said this raises concern about how the yen may react.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Meanwhile sterling was mostly flat against the dollar at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par $1.5812\tab   after the Bank of England left Britain's repo\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rate unchanged at 6.0 percent on Thursday as expected.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par BoE Governor Eddie George said all Monetary Policy\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Committee members would be happier with the pound at a lower\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par level while MPC member DeAnne Julius said it was unwise to keep\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par raising rates without evidence that sterling was falling.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((U.S. Financial Markets Desk, 212 859 1690)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw3904xv7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
