\par\par \b \uc2  Yen falls, traders cite wariness of BOJ action. \b0\par\par\uc2 240 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 09:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, March 9 (Reuters) - The yen racked up speedy losses against the dollar and the euro early in Europe on Thursday with traders citing wariness of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Concern that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  could sell yen during European hours was fanned after Japanese Vince Finance Minister Nobuaki Usui said during Asian hours that the authorities had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in overseas \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The yen's latest losses were triggered after Usui followed up these comments by saying there was no change in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy of using decisive \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  when needed. \par \par \uc2  "We have just gone up on the back of these comments as the market is very jumpy about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a trader at a U.S. bank in London. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan sold yen for dollars during Asian hours on Wednesday. Bankers in Tokyo said on Thursday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had also sold yen for euros during European hours a day ago but that such sales were not conducted through the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar rose a 1/3 of a yen within minutes to peaks just shy of 107 while the euro sped up to highs near 103 yen from levels around 102.65/70 in the wake of Usui's comments. \par \par \uc2  ((Swaha Pattanaik, London Capital Markets, +44 171 542 6284, swaha.pattanaik@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  