\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro bounces ahead but gains may not last. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Genevieve Wilkinson \par \uc2 829 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 19:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, March 9 (Reuters) - The euro bounced higher on Thursday, rising more than three quarters of a percent against the dollar and reversing losses against the yen as dealers adjusted positions in the wake of recent heavy selling. \par \par \uc2  At the same time the yen held firm against the dollar, trading up more than half a percent at noon, buoyed by stronger than expected Japanese economic data, ongoing repatriation of funds before Tokyo's year end and disappointment over Wall Street's sluggish bounce higher. \par \par \uc2  "The move this morning has been in euro/yen which seems to be the only thing that is really trading these days," said Ralph DelZenero, vice president at Banc One Capital Markets in Chicago. \par \par \uc2  The euro was around 103.23 yen in early afternoon, a full yen up from critical support levels. \par \par \uc2  Traders were seen buying euros after several sessions of heavy selling, in part because the decline may have gone too far and also in the wake of some optimism about Europe's recovery. \par \par \uc2  The euro was boosted not only on technical sentiment but also by news that growth in the 11 nation euro zone rose 0.9 percent in the fourth quarter. Hawkish comments on Wednesday from European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Vice President Christian Noyer also helped the euro. \par \par \uc2  "Q4 pan-European data was seen by the market as being euro bullish," said Paul Podolsky at FleetBoston. \par \par \uc2  However most analysts said the euro would not break out of a downtrend unless it topped 97.50 cents and that the ailing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  which hits successive record lows only a few weeks ago may soon slide again. \par \par \uc2  SLUGGISH U.S. STOCKS WEIGH ON DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar's weakness against the euro could be blamed in part on soft U.S. equity markets. \par \par \uc2  The Dow Jones industrial average was nearly flat shortly after noon, trading at 9856 just one day after a partial recovery from a mammoth sell-off on Tuesday. The Nasdaq composite index gained 1.50 percent in early afternoon trade. \par \par \uc2  "When U.S. stocks get near these critical levels and they don't bounce substantially, it makes people marginally nervous," Podolsky said. \par \par \uc2  The yen also gained on the dollar in the wake of news that Japan's core private sector machinery orders rose 0.8 percent in January, far outstripping analysts calls for a 7.7 percent drop. \par \par \uc2  But the yen's gains were constrained because traders were still on amber alert for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  one day after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold yen for dollars during Asian hours on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The nervousness about another round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  grew amid talk that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had also sold yen again during the European day on Wednesday. Traders could not confirm this and many found it odd that the Bank of Japan would have ignored protocol by not conducting its \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  through the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  or the Bank of England. \par \par \uc2  On the other hand because the Bank of Japan had no obvious help from its partner nations, dealers may be bold and try to push the yen up more. \par \par \uc2  "The BoJ is alone on this and the market knows that," Podolsky said. "It would be entirely different if they'd \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the ECB or with someone else. That tempts the market to test them." \par \par \uc2  Analysts are already bracing for a soft fourth quarter gross domestic product report due out of Japan on Monday. Such a report would technically put Japan back into recession and analysts said this raises concern about how the yen may react. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile sterling was flat against the dollar at $1.58 after the Bank of England left Britain's repo rate unchanged at 6.0 percent on Thursday as expected. \par \par \uc2  BoE Governor Eddie George said all Monetary Policy Committee members would be happier with the pound at a lower level while MPC member DeAnne Julius said it was unwise to keep raising rates without evidence that sterling was falling. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 1755GMT.  All data taken from Reuters with percent \par \par \uc2  change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab    Last     US Close  %Chg   YTD %  1999 Cls\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab 08 Mar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/dlr\tab \tab    0.9676   0.9605   +0.74   -3.91   1.0070\par Dlr/yen\tab \tab     106.60   107.21   -0.57   +4.30   102.21\par Euro/yen\tab \tab    103.11   102.98   +0.13   +0.01   103.10\par Dlr/swiss\tab \tab   1.6604   1.6716   -0.67   +4.41   1.5902\par Stg/dlr\tab \tab     1.5806   1.5803   +0.02   -2.29   1.6176\par Can/dlr\tab \tab     1.4581   1.4561   +0.14   +0.87   1.4455\par Aus/dlr\tab \tab     0.6150   0.6086   +1.05   -6.29   0.6563\par Euro/swiss\tab \tab  1.6067   1.6062   +0.03   +0.19   1.6036\par Euro/stg\tab \tab    0.6116   0.6073   +0.71   -1.97   0.6239.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw3904tqj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex1