\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  jitters limit yen gains. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sabrina Ghani \par \uc2 646 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 09:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, March 9 (Reuters) - The yen made limited headway on Thursday amid wariness after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  a day ago, although strong Japanese economic data were seen providing support to the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Concern that the Bank of Japan could sell yen during European hours was fanned after Japanese Vice Finance Minister Nobuaki Usui said during Asian hours that the authorities had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in overseas \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The yen racked up speedy losses but remained above New York's close after Usui followed up these comments in Europe on Thursday by saying there was no change in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy of using decisive \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  when needed. \par \par \uc2  "The Japanese manufacturing orders have been pretty strong, but there are rumours that the BOJ came in yesterday after the Tokyo close and the same could happen today so people are hesitant to sell euro/yen, dollar/yen," said Klaus Kusber, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Dresdner Kleinwort Benson in Frankfurt. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan sold yen for dollars during Asian hours on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Bankers in Tokyo said on Thursday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had also sold yen for euros during European hours a day ago but that such sales were not conducted through the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar was hovering near the day's lows around 106.60 yen JPY=), down from 107.21 yen in U.S. trade late on Wednesday, but up about a yen from Tuesday's one-month low of 105.73. \par \par \uc2  The euro EURJPY=) was pinned just below 103 yen, little changed from the U.S. close of 102.98 yen on Wednesday but firmly above Tuesday's record low of 100.90. \par \par \uc2  Earlier in Tokyo, the Vice Finance Minister Nobuaki Usui confirmed that the BOJ sold yen in Europe on Wednesday, but declined to identify whether it was against the euro or the dollar. \par \par \uc2  He also reiterated that Japan will continue to take decisive steps in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if needed. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, Japan's core private-sector machinery orders, excluding orders for machinery at electric power companies and for ships, showed a seasonally-adjusted rise of 0.8 percent in January from the previous month. The data, considered a leading indicator for capital spending, dwarfed a median forecast of a 7.7 percent decline in a Reuters poll 14 economists. \par \par \uc2  The data came after a \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  corporate survey for October-December showed capital spending by Japanese firms dipping by less than expected in the last three months of 1999. \par \par \uc2  Spending was down only 0.7 percent from a year earlier, compared to forecasts for a 1.0 to 6.0 percent fall. \par \par \uc2  EURO BOLSTERED BY NOYER COMMENTS \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the euro rebounded from one and a half week lows it set against the dollar in the previous session after the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  vice president Christian Noyer said late on Wednesday that eurozone growth in 2000 and 2001 could be higher than three percent. \par \par \uc2  He also said that inflation would be below two percent in the same period. \par \par \uc2  "We had some hawkish comments from Noyer yesterday," said Jeremy Hawkins, chief economic adviser at the Bank of America. \par \par \uc2  "Inflation risks are on the upside and it's possible the ECB may move next week, so near-term it's slightly more positive for the euro." \par \par \uc2  Traders said that there was still volatility and nervousness in the U.S. equity market and that is why euro/dollar was biased towards testing the upper-end of the recent trading range. They said that if the euro breaches $0.9670, that would be very bullish. \par \par \uc2  Against the dollar, the euro EUR=) was pinned about a quarter cent above $0.96, up more than a cent from Wednesday's one and a half week low of $0.9519. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw3904pi1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
