\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar slips as  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  nerves linger. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Chikafumi Hodo \par \uc2 967 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 04:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, March 9 (Reuters) - The dollar drifted below 107 yen by midday on Thursday in Tokyo, reacting to some bright signs for Japan's economy, but its fall was limited by the prospect of further BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the yen in check. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 106.80/90 yen, compared with 107.21 yen in U.S. trade late on Wednesday, having moved in a tight range of 106.87 to 107.27 yen. \par \par \uc2  News that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had followed through on its yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Tokyo on Wednesday by later stepping into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in European hours provided the euro with a firm footing. \par \par \uc2  Bankers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had bought euroS for yen and the Finance Ministry later confirmed it had taken "necessary steps" in overseas trade. \par \par \uc2  "The yen-buying mood is still there, but many dealers do not have the courage to drive the dollar below 106.70 yen on caution over BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a Japanese city bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "The market is very careful about building yen-longs now, but the momentum to push the yen higher is clearly picking up." \par \par \uc2  The market is focusing on Japan's October-December gross domestic product data due out on Monday, with expectations of an improved figure growing after Thursday's stronger-than-expected capital spending by Japanese firms, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday that firms cut spending on plant and equipment by 0.7 percent in the October-December quarter from the same period a year earlier. \par \par \uc2  It was the eighth straight quarter in which capital investment at all firms had dipped from a year earlier, but it was a sharp improvement over the 9.6 percent drop in July-September. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar stayed under pressure after the data, but many participants were reluctant to sell it actively. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said overseas operators were showing strong needs to unwind their dollar-long positions against the yen. Such sales should put a lid to the greenback above 107 yen. \par \par \uc2  Sales by Japanese exporters were expected to emerge between 107.50 and 108 yen. Strong support was seen at 106.50 yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But yen-buying could by spurred if the Nikkei average advances further in the afternoon. The stock market benchmark rose 118.74 points or 0.60 percent to 19,885.54 by midday. \par \par \uc2  Finance Ministry data showed on Thursday that Japanese investors sold a net 272.6 billion yen of foreign bonds, based on contracts, in February, compared with net sales of 476.0 billion yen a month earlier. Meanwhile, foreigners bought a net 859.6 billion yen in Japanese stocks. \par \par \uc2  The euro was under selling pressure, with resistance seen around 103.20 yen, but falls were likely to be limited on caution over the possible BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Vice Finance Minister Nobuaki Usui told Reuters that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market overseas on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  He said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to take decisive steps in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if needed. \par \par \uc2  Bankers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had acted alone in the European market on Wednesday by buying the euro, possibly when it dipped below 102 yen. \par \par \uc2  The euro fell to around a low of 101.70 yen in Europe on Wednesday, but rebounded sharply to around 103 yen. \par \par \uc2  At 0313 GMT, the euro was quoted at 102.80/90 yen compared with a U.S. close of 102.98 yen on Wednesday. The euro stood at $0.9620/25 compared with $0.9605. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the Australian dollar rose after employment data came in above a market consensus. \par \par \uc2  February employment grew by 59,100 jobs, while the unemployment rate was at 6.7 percent compared with market expectations of a rise of 25,000 jobs and the jobless rate at 6.8 percent. \par \par \uc2  At 0332 GMT, the Aussie stood at $0.6127/32 from a U.S. close of $0.6086. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0335 GMT.  All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 \par \par \uc2  GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab      Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   1999 Cls\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   08 Mar.\par \tab \tab \tab      -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr\tab \tab     0.9620   0.9605   +0.18    -4.45   1.0070\par  Dlr/yen\tab \tab      106.79   107.21   -0.39    +4.48   102.21\par  Euro/yen\tab \tab     102.74   102.98   -0.13    -0.24   103.10\par  Dlr/swiss\tab \tab    1.6696   1.6716   -0.22    +4.89   1.5902\par  Stg/dlr\tab \tab      1.5801   1.5803   -0.01    -2.31   1.6176\par  Can/dlr\tab \tab      1.4551   1.4561   -0.07    +0.66   1.4455\par  Aus/dlr\tab \tab      0.6128   0.6086   +0.69    -6.63   0.6563\par  Euro/swiss\tab \tab   1.6064   1.6062   +0.01    +0.17   1.6036\par  Euro/stg\tab \tab     0.6084   0.6073   +0.25    -2.42   0.6239.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 0335 GMT.  All data taken from Reuters\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2