\par\par \b \uc2  CORRECTED-FOCUS-BOJ rare euro buying shows economy fears. \b0\par\par\uc2 666 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 11:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  In TOKYO story headlined FOCUS-BOJ rare euro buying shows economy fears please read in 5th para ...Nobuaki Usui... instead of ...Mobuaki Usui... (correcting spelling) \par \par \uc2  A corrected version follows. \par \par \uc2  By Chikafumi Hodo \par \par \uc2  TOKYO, March 9 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rare overnight \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy euros against the yen, and without help from its European counterpart, underlines its determination to curb the yen to try to ensure economic recovery, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The bank did not put its euro purchase orders through the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , meaning it took the unusual measure of acting alone to support the euro, bankers said. \par \par \uc2  The apparent unwillingness of the ECB to help out appeared to signal that the embattled single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could weaken further in European trading. \par \par \uc2  It was the second time in 24 hours the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the first time to buy dollars in Tokyo trading hours. \par \par \uc2  "We took necessary action overseas yesterday for the sake of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability," Vice Finance Minister Nobuaki Usui told Reuters. "Our stance that we will continue taking decisive steps if needed has not changed." \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, the BOJ bought dollars at around 106.30 yen, sending the dollar advancing above 107.50 yen and helping the euro to clear 103 yen. \par \par \uc2  However, the euro fell again in European trading hours to as low as 101.70 yen, around which point the BOJ stepped in, prompting its sharp rebound to around 103 yen. The BOJ has twice before \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  during European trading to buy euros against the yen, once through the ECB and once acting alone. \par \par \uc2  The euro was still struggling at 102.60/70 yen in late Tokyo from a U.S. close of 102.98 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "The government has repeatedly said the yen's rise would hinder economic growth so they want to prevent any resurgence in the yen," a senior European dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Sentiment for the euro has deteriorated since late February when comments by ECB officials extinguished expectations it might raise rates to halt the relentless weakening in the year-old \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Speculative selling pressure on the euro has also picked up momentum against the yen since last week, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  FEARS INSURERS MAY GO UNDER ON EURO WEAKNESS \par \par \uc2  However, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , for which the BOJ acts as an agent, wants a stable euro against the yen, particularly before institutional investors close their books at the end of March. \par \par \uc2  Many of Japan's troubled life insurers have taken trillions of yen worth of euro positions and are facing huge, and potentially back-breaking, losses as the year-end approaches. \par \par \uc2  They must write off losses incurred by investment in unlisted foreign securities if these exceed more than 15 percent in yen terms as of March 31. \par \par \uc2  The dollar has lost about 11 percent against the yen since the end of last March, while the euro had depreciated 22 percent when it touched a low of 100.95 yen on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "There has been constant speculation that the BOJ would help these investors because further weakness in the euro could bury them," a Japanese commercial bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will indeed help them, but I don't think it was the major reason the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight," he said. "Saving the insurers doesn't necessarily mean such a move would help the overall economy." \par \par \uc2  Japanese exporters have been groaning at the strength of the yen and officials are eager to see a stronger upturn in trade to help to fuel a self-sustaining recovery from Japan's worst recession in half a century. \par \par \uc2  Japan exported 8.46 trillion yen worth of products to the European Union in calendar 1999, compared with 14.61 trillion yen to the United States and 17.71 trillion yen to Asia. But Japan's exports to Asia are 50 percent denominated in yen. \par \par \uc2  ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432-8785 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw3904o5e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
