\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr Eases Against Yen On Fund-Selling \b0\par\par\uc2  By Nick Shindo \par \uc2 936 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 06:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The dollar drifted lower against the yen in Asian trading Thursday on selling by U.S. technical funds, but lingering concerns over a possible fresh bout of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was enough to keep most bearish accounts at bay. \par \par \uc2  The euro recovered slightly against the dollar and edged lower against the yen in thin trading, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  After Wednesday's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the BOJ sent the dollar flying up to around Y107.50, the day's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading was understandably marked by caution, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Traders for once appeared to take heed of senior Finance Ministry official Zembei Mizoguchi's warning early Thursday that Japanese monetary authorities are "watching markets closely" and "will take proper action as needed." \par \par \uc2  With the dollar apparently hemmed in against the yen, a largely listless market saw the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  move in a narrow range between Y106.63 and Y107.27, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  As the day went on, technical sales orders from market model-type U.S. funds pushed the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gradually lower, not far off key support at Y106.50, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Even news late in the session that January machinery orders lept by an impressively strong 0.8% over December had a limited impact as traders' caution snuffed out any instinct to go longer yen, dealers said. The market had expected orders to fall 8.1%. \par \par \uc2  However, the fact that market players still had the stomach to sell the dollar well into Y106 territory, despite the haunting presence of the BOJ, reflects continued heavy sentiment, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Pressure looks likely to stay on the dollar at least until Monday's GDP data. It's possible that the market could get a nasty negative shock that may spark a rush to the dollar," said a senior trader at Sanwa Bank. \par \par \uc2  Japanese investors were also said to have selling interest on dollar upticks to around Y107.50, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT (12:15 a.m. EST), the dollar was quoted at Y106.85, below Y107.23 late Wednesday in New York. The dollar was at Y107.20 late Wednesday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $0.9623, higher than $0.9607 late Wednesday in New York. The euro was at $0.9583 in Tokyo Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y102.82, down from Y103.02 in New York late Wednesday. The euro was at Y102.73 in Tokyo late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Underlining the lack of momentum in markets Thursday, the release earlier in the day of two encouraging economic surveys by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  had little impact on trading. \par \par \uc2  Capital investment during the October-December quarter fell 0.7% on-year, the ministry said in one report. This compared favorably with year-on-year declines of 9.6% in the July-September period and 13.4% in the three months to June. \par \par \uc2  The other report showed that business sentiment continues to brighten. The ministry's business sentiment index for large companies in the January to March quarter improved to plus 4.9 from plus 1.5 three months earlier. \par \par \uc2  Takehiro Sato, an economist at Morgan Stanley Dean Witter, said the relatively strong investment data - which came in better than most had expected - could encourage analysts to revise their October-December GDP estimates to show a slower pace of contraction. \par \par \uc2  He said the unexpectedly good fixed investment data is forcing the investment house to reassess its present forecast for October-December gross domestic product due Monday. \par \par \uc2  "We may be forced to upgrade our quarter-on-quarter forecast of minus 1.6% by 0.1% or 0.2%," he said. \par \par \uc2  And if relatively strong capital spending for that period can help GDP better the market's average expectation of a 1.2% fall, the net result could be further yen buying against the dollar in the near-term - even if the economy contracts further into a technical recession, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  More generally, the dollar's upside continues to be temporarily capped by talk of further Japanese repatriation of overseas funds ahead of fiscal-year end Mar. 31, some dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Inherent weakness in the euro/yen - which was the subject of vicious speculative selling earlier this week - is also encouraging sales in other yen-cross \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , others noted. \par \par \uc2  At the same time, the threat of further Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to provide a solid floor to both the dollar and euro against the yen for the weeks to come. \par \par \uc2  "The BOJ will come up again and again as it deems fit in the days ahead of fiscal year-end in Japan," in an effort to mitigate \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  book losses suffered by Japanese corporations, said Shuji Takano, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at ABN-Amro Bank in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Looking ahead, traders will be watching the outcome of the Bank of England's policy committee later in the session for any possible change in key lending rates although the majority view backs a "no-change" outcome. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.5805, down from $1.5813 in New York late Wednesday. Sterling was at $1.5792 in Tokyo late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  -By Nick Shindo; 813-5255-2929; nick.shindo@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates which accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture which is updated hourly. \par \par \uc2  Subscribers can find this table: \par \par \uc2  -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087. \par \par \uc2  -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX \par \par \uc2  -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT \par \par \uc2  -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw3901a4d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
