\par\par \b \uc2  MOF Mizoguchi: Watching  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Mkts Closely \b0\par\par\uc2 149 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 01:05\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- A day after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to stem the yen's rise, the director-general of the international bureau at Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  reiterated Thursday that the ministry remains on alert. \par \par \uc2  Asked about Wednesday's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Zembei Mizoguchi told reporters, "We are watching the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets closely, and will take appropriate measures as needed." \par \par \uc2  Traders said the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  around mid-morning Wednesday, selling yen and buying dollars first between Y106.30-Y106.40 and then again around Y107.00. Some traders said there were rumors that the BOJ was also buying the euro against the yen. \par \par \uc2  Japan's vice finance minister for international affairs Haruhiko Kuroda confirmed the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  later Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Thursday morning around 0010 GMT (7:10 p.m. EST), the dollar was trading around Y107.10. \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw39019xa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
