\par\par \b \uc2  Yen bulls run for cover after  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tamawa Kadoya \par \uc2 963 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 09:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, March 8 (Reuters) - The yen was hovering lower against the dollar in late afternoon trade in Tokyo on Wednesday following \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem its rise after it bounded to a five-week high overnight. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's unexpected action, its first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since January 4, pushed the dollar up by over one yen to 107.50 yen from an earlier low of 106.02 yen and helped to boost the embattled euro to 103.15 yen from around 101.70 yen in early trade. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said the bid to hold back the yen could be shortlived, and the dollar, still seen under pressure to weaken after Wall Street dipped nearly four percent overnight, could see further losses. \par \par \uc2  "Without other central banks participating, these are going to be little more than smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Larry Duke, vice president at Citibank in Tokyo, told Reuters Television. \par \par \uc2  "You'll get a bounce in the short term, but then the fundamentals come back in," he said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Bank of Japan (BOJ), which acts as the government's agent, was detected buying dollars for yen around 106.30 yen to 106.80 yen. It was also rumoured to be buying above 107 yen. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs, Haruhiko Kuroda, confirmed the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "We are watching (\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) movements," he said. \par \par \uc2  But he declined to comment on which \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was targeted by the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , ordered by Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was quoted at 107.19/29 yen compared with 106.07 yen in late U.S. trade on Tuesday. The euro was at 102.74/87 yen versus 101.77 yen in Tuesday's late U.S. trade. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unlikely to have bought euros for yen during Wednesday's session, despite some speculation that the euro's recent sharp falls would prompt the Japanese authorities to prop up the European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The euro tumbled to a fresh lifetime low of 100.95 yen in overseas trade on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ directly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last year in defence of the euro on a couple of occasions, but the action did not find favour with the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which was keeping a strictly hands off approach to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  management. \par \par \uc2  Only two days ago, Bundesbank President Ernst Welteke flatly stated that short-term measures could not stabilise the euro. \par \par \uc2  And on Tuesday, Miyazawa said that European nations seem not very concerned about recent weakness in the euro. \par \par \uc2  Moreover, dealers said buying euros for yen would not be effective without euro-buying, dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Much of the problem is euro weakness not yen strength, and there's not a lot the Bank of Japan can do about that," a U.S. bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Market participants suspected that Japanese authorities were concerned that further weakness in the euro against the yen would put further downward pressure on the dollar versus yen. \par \par \uc2  "(Japanese) monetary authorities would not want to see the dollar going below 105 yen, and wanted to prevent that before it was too late," said Noriyoshi Tsunoda, manager and chief dealer at Fuji Bank's International Treasury Division. \par \par \uc2  Buying dollars for yen would indirectly help buoy the euro against the yen. \par \par \uc2  The dollar remained about one yen higher in late Tokyo trade, but steady selling interest near 107.50 yen will likely cap gains despite the BOJ's dollar-buying action. \par \par \uc2  "There is still selling interest from some major U.S. fund operators and also from Japanese exporters who have offers lined up above 108 yen," a trust bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ Policy Board decided to leave monetary policy unchanged, exactly in line with market expectations. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the euro was little changed against the dollar. The euro was at $0.9604/06 compared with $0.9592 in late U.S. trade on Tuesday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0728 GMT. All data taken from Reuters with \par \par \uc2  percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab      Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   1999 Cls\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   07 Mar.\par \tab \tab \tab      -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr\tab \tab     0.9603   0.9592   +0.11    -4.64   1.0070\par  Dlr/yen\tab \tab      107.04   106.07   +0.91    +4.73   102.21\par  Euro/yen\tab \tab     102.72   101.77   +0.93    -0.37   103.10\par  Dlr/swiss\tab \tab    1.6720   1.6744   -0.14    +5.14   1.5902\par  Stg/dlr\tab \tab      1.5802   1.5793   +0.06    -2.31   1.6176\par  Can/dlr\tab \tab      1.4557   1.4544   +0.09    +0.71   1.4455\par  Aus/dlr\tab \tab      0.6063   0.6055   +0.13    -7.62   0.6563\par  Euro/swiss\tab \tab   1.6062   1.6071   -0.06    +0.16   1.6036\par  Euro/stg\tab \tab     0.6077   0.6060   +0.28    -2.60   0.6239.\par \f28 \p