\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen claws back from  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  lows. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Daniel Sternoff \par \uc2 843 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 18:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, March 8 (Reuters) - The yen tiptoed higher in New York on Wednesday, paring losses suffered in Asia when the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to yank the yen from Tuesday's all-time highs against the euro and five-week peaks against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  surprised the market overnight, buying dollars for yen for the second time this year, forcing the yen to a low of 107.50 per dollar and 103.19 per euro. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say the BoJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , ordered by Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa, was aimed at smoothing the yen's rapid ascent which threatened to become unruly ahead of the end of Japan's fiscal year this month. \par \par \uc2  But the BoJ's action failed to reverse the market's momentum, as dealers bid the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  back to hover little more than one yen away from its Tuesday peaks of 105.73 yen per dollar and 100.90 yen per euro. \par \par \uc2  "Whenever you seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  it's only good for a short period of time, and then we go back to basics again," said John Schein, vice president at Fortis USA. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In midday New York trade, the dollar extended its decline from post-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  highs to around 106.75 yen\tab  .\par The euro slipped as far as the 101.75 yen area, but traders nervous the Bank of Japan may step in again pushed the single \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  back to trade around 102.25 yen\tab      at midday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I would think they'll show their hand again," said Seth Garrett, global head of spot trading at Credit Suisse First Boston. "I would think (the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) is not a one-off thing."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts said officials in Tokyo, who have expressed concerns that yen strength may hurt prospects for economic recovery, had acted to manage the yen's rapid rise from six-month lows against the dollar and four-month floors against the euro just two weeks ago.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I think what is clear is they are concerned about euro/yen levels, particularly as we approach 100. We know that in the past they have been worried about dollar/yen as well," said Tim Fox, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at Standard Chartered Bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts doubt, however, that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  can fight fundamentally-driven market flows.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I would argue that the move over the last couple of weeks was triggered by unwinding of overly negative expectations on Japan's economy," said Jim McCormick, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at J.P. Morgan in New York.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Other market watchers have linked the yen's rise to the approaching end of the Japanese fiscal year, when Japanese firms have historically repatriated overseas funds.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro, meanwhile, faced fresh selling pressure against the dollar after weaker than expected German manufacturing data overnight reinforced sour sentiment on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro drooped to a week low of 95.24 cents, dangling some 1-1/2 cents above its record floor, before rebounding to the 95.70 cent  area at midday as traders took profits and wobbling U.S. stock markets raised some concerns about the dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "You've got to be worried about the euro," said Standard Chartered's Fox, noting that the single \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had failed to benefit from data showing German unemployment fell for the fifth month in a row.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro also failed to benefit from verbal support from Bank of France Governor Jean-Claude Trichet and the French and German finance ministers.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "European officials have been talking the euro up since it was at $1.08 any observer can see it's had no effect," said a trader at a U.S. bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We want to see some corroboration of an uptrend and a pick up in business in Europe," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((U.S. Financial Markets Desk, 212 859 1690)).\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 12:36 p.m. (1736 GMT). All data taken\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from Reuters with percent change calculated from the daily U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par close at 4:30 p.m. (2130 GMT).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab    Last     US Close  %Chg   YTD %    1999\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab Mar 07\tab \tab \tab   Close\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/dlr\tab \tab    0.9571   0.9592   -0.22   -4.96   1.0070\par Dlr/yen\tab \tab     106.77   106.07   +0.66   +4.46   102.21\par Euro/yen\tab \tab    102.22   101.77   +0.44   -0.85   103.10\par Dlr/swiss\tab \tab   1.6766   1.6744   +0.13   +5.43   1.5902\par Stg/dlr\tab \tab     1.5842   1.5793   +0.31   -2.06   1.6176\par Can/dlr\tab \tab     1.4588   1.4544   +0.30   +0.92   1.4455\par Aus/dlr\tab 