\par\par \b \uc2  Japan took action in  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 , watching market - Kuroda. \b0\par\par\uc2 237 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 05:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, March 8 (Reuters) - Senior Finance Ministry official Haruhiko Kuroda on Wednesday confirmed that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market after the dollar jumped more than one yen in early morning Tokyo trade. \par \par \uc2  Asked to confirm talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the yen's rise against the dollar on Wednesday, Kuroda told reporters: "We took appropriate action in the market." \par \par \uc2  But he declined to comment on which \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was targeted by the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Finance Ministry instructs the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  acts in the market on behalf of the Finance Ministry. \par \par \uc2  Asked his view of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Kuroda, vice finance minister for international affairs, said: "We are watching movements." \par \par \uc2  Asked about the weakness of the euro, Kuroda said: "\b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements should reflect fundamentals. That's all I can say." \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was initially detected buying dollars for yen at between 106.30 yen to 106.80 yen. It was also rumoured to be buying dollars above 107 yen. \par \par \uc2  Following the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar jumped as high as 107.50 yen from 106.02 yen in early trade in Tokyo. The euro also jumped against the yen, reaching 102.95 yen from 101.75 yen. \par \par \uc2  ((Yoko Nishikawa, Tokyo Newsroom +81-3 3432 8022 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw3804x45\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
