\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen stabilises above post- \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  lows. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Lisa Jucca \par \uc2 573 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 14:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, March 8 (Reuters) - The yen recovered some sparkle after the shock of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday and was trying to build a base above the lows set against the euro and the dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold yen for dollars for the second confirmed time this year earlier in Asia, pushing the yen to a low of around 107.50 to the dollar JPY=). Euro/yen rose in tandem with dollar/yen, zooming above 103 yen EURJPY=). \par \par \uc2  But by 1300 GMT, the yen had regained half a yen against the dollar and 3/4 yen against the euro and was stabilising around these levels, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "The BOJ was aiming at stabilising the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," sais Jane Foley, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Barclays Capital in London. \par \par \uc2  "Although it has failed to weaken significantly the yen, we are seeing more stable conditions this morning, so it has not been completely ineffective." \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the BOJ resolved to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  after Tuesday's euro/yen slide to a record below 101 and a slide in dollar/yen to a five-week low of 105.73. They viewed the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a signal from Japanese authorities that they would not tolerate further yen appreciation ahead of Japan's fiscal year end. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs, Haruhiko Kuroda, confirmed there had been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but declined to comment on which \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was targeted by the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , ordered by Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa. \par \par \uc2  Although the yen seemed to have regained some strength, analysts said traders would be wary of betting too hard on the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , particularly against the frail euro, for fears the BOJ might step in again soon. \par \par \uc2  "It's certainly possible that we will see further action," said Derek Halpenny, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi in London. \par \par \uc2  "Maintaining euro/yen at levels above 100 is something the BOJ wants to do." \par \par \uc2  BROAD EURO WEAKNESS DRAGS EURO/YEN LOWER \par \par \uc2  Analysts said euro/yen was looking particularly vulnerable as it had dropped to record lows just a day earlier and it was put under pressure by the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's persistent weakness against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The euro was put under pressure across the board in Europe after German manufacturing orders dipped unexpectedly by 0.4 percent in January from December. West German orders fell 0.5 percent in January from December on a seasonally adjusted basis. \par \par \uc2  The report dragged the euro to within 1/4 cent of Tuesday's $0.9524 EUR=) one-week lows after the release. \par \par \uc2  Earlier in Europe the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had remained steady after official German seasonally adjusted jobless total fell 34,000 in February from January, confirming an earlier leak. \par \par \uc2  Remarks by Bank of France Governor Jean-Claude Trichet, who reiterated the euro has potential to appreciate, failed to lift the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But minor support was offered to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by a joint statement by French and German finance ministers in Frech paper Le Mond saying they want a stronger euro. \par \par \uc2  Despite persistent euro weakness, analysts did not expect the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to go beyond verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its effort to support the euro. \par \par \uc2  "If \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unsuccessful, it can damage the credibility of a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Foley at Barclays Capital. \par \par \uc2  "Therefore it is not something the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will go into lightly." \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw3804wwl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
