\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen creeps up after BoJ  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Daniel Sternoff \par \uc2 769 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 15:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, March 8 (Reuters) - The yen edged cautiously higher in New York on Wednesday after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia to yank the yen below Tuesday's all-time high against the euro and five-week peaks against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  surprised the market in Asian trading hours, buying dollars for yen for the second time this year, forcing the yen to a low of 107.50 per dollar and 103.19 per euro. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say the BoJ was acting to smooth the yen's rapid ascent which threatened to become unruly ahead of the end of Japan's fiscal year this month. \par \par \uc2  The yen eased off its lows in European hours and tiptoed higher in early New York, returning to around one yen away from its Tuesday peaks of 105.73 yen per dollar and 100.90 yen per euro, but caution prevailed over further market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "If history means anything, one would expect a little consolidation and then another test to the downside because the forces moving the yen stronger aren't going to disappear due to a bout of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a trader at a U.S. bank. \par \par \uc2  "It would take several bouts of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the trader added. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs, Haruhiko Kuroda, confirmed there had been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but declined to comment on which \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was targeted by the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , ordered by Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In early New York, the dollar edged below 107 yen\tab   while the euro slipped through the 102 yen\tab      support area.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Jim McCormick, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at J.P. Morgan in New York, said the Bank of Japan had acted to smooth the yen's rapid rise from six-month lows against the dollar and four-month floors against the euro just two weeks ago.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The yen was moving to fast in illiquid and risk averse markets," McCormick said, adding that the Bank of Japan has been ineffective at halting fundamentally driven market moves.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I would argue that the move over the last couple of weeks was triggered by unwinding of overly negative expectations on Japan's economy," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro, dangling less than 1-1/2 cents above its record lows against the dollar, faced fresh selling pressure after German manufacturing orders dipped unexpectedly by 0.4 percent in December, falling well short of market expectations.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The weak numbers out of Germany are going to drop the euro lower, and the sense is that the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said Alan Kabbani, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trader at First Union National Bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In early New York, the euro slipped to one-week lows of 95.24 cents   .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But traders said they were cautious about selling the euro too heavily, feeling that further weakness against the yen could prompt the Bank of Japan to step in again.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Earlier in Europe the single \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had remained steady after official German seasonally adjusted jobless total fell 34,000 in February from January, confirming an earlier leak.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Remarks by Bank of France Governor Jean-Claude Trichet, who reiterated the euro has potential to appreciate, failed to lift the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The French and German finance ministers also offered verbal support to the euro in the French paper Le Monde.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((U.S. Financial Markets Desk, 212 859 1690)).\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 9:32 a.m. (1432 GMT). All data taken\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from Reuters with percent change calculated from the daily U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par close at 4:30 p.m. (2130 GMT).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab    Last     US Close  %Chg   YTD %    1999\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab Mar 07\tab \tab \tab   Close\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/dlr\tab \tab    0.9532   0.9592   -0.63   -5.34   1.0070\par Dlr/yen\tab \tab     106.86   106.07   +0.74   +4.55   102.21\par Euro/yen\tab \tab    101.84   101.77   +0.07   -1.22   103.10\par Dlr/swiss\tab \tab   1.6834   1.6744   +0.54   +5.86   1.5902\par Stg/dlr\tab \tab     1.5752   1.5793   -0.26   -2.62   1.6176\par Can/dlr\tab \tab     1.4596   1.4544   +0.36   +0.98   1.4455\par Aus/dlr\tab \tab     0.6068   0.6055   +0.21   -7.54   0.6563\par Euro/swiss\tab \tab  1.6054   1.6071   -0.11   +0.11   1.6036\par Euro/stg\tab \tab    0.6052   0.6060   -0.13   -3.00   0.6239\par  All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news ...\tab     Debt...   Indicators...\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports..\ta