\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  - Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention \highlight\uc2  forces yen lower. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sabrina Ghani \par \uc2 483 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 09:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, March 8 (Reuters) - The yen fell across the board on Wednesday after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time in two months in the foreign exchanges. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sales of yen for dollars pushed the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  up by over one yen to around 107.50 yen from the five-week low of 105.73 hit on Tuesday. The euro capitalised on the yen's weakness and rallied as high as 103.06 yen from the record lows around 100.90 hit a day ago. \par \par \uc2  "The BOJ has an eye on the 105/106 yen area and wants to make sure that remains intact on the downside because if we go through this area it will be a dangerous development," said Ian Gunner, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN Amro Bank in London. \par \par \uc2  "We are back at 107 (in dollar/yen), so \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not have much impact but it will make the market fairly cautious." \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 107.20/23 yen, while the euro was 102.91/04 yen at 0827 GMT. \par \par \uc2  BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  TARGETS DOLLAR/YEN \par \par \uc2  Traders in Tokyo said the BOJ, which acts as the government's agent, was detected buying dollars for yen around 106.30 yen to 106.80 yen. It was also rumoured to be buying above 107 yen. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs, Haruhiko Kuroda, confirmed there had been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but declined to comment on which \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was targeted by the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , ordered by Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in euro/yen despite some speculation that the euro's recent sharp falls would prompt the Japanese authorities to prop up the euro, which tumbled to a fresh lifetime low of 100.95 yen on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ directly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last year to curb the yen against the euro on at least one occasion. Dealers said any fresh \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on euro/yen would not be effective if central banks did not buy euros for dollars as well. \par \par \uc2  "Much of the problem is euro weakness not yen strength, and there's not a lot the Bank of Japan can do about that," a U.S. bank dealer in Tokyo said. \par \par \uc2  Traders said they did not necessarily expect the U.S. Federal Reserve to join forces and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  at current levels. It would take dollar losses towards 100 yen before that became a more likely scenario, they said. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the euro was little changed against the dollar, showing little immediate reaction after sources said that Pan-European February jobless would drop 34,000 from January. Official data was due out at 0900 GMT. The euro was hovering around $0.96, up from the one-week low of $0.9524 set on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw3804rjv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
