\par\par \b \uc2  ECB seen in no hurry to join BOJ in  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 583 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 14:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, March 8 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may return to the foreign exchanges to curb yen strength against the euro and the dollar, but the euro's fall is unlikely to bring offers of help from the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts said on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ launched its first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in two months on Wednesday, selling the yen a day after it hit record highs of 100.90 per euro and five-week highs around 105.80 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  While the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars for yen in Asia, euro/yen losses have been the main driving force for the yen's latest export-crippling surge, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The weaker euro was also perceived as a concern for euro zone policymakers, but the ECB was expected to be reluctant to use \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "If the BOJ will do its dirty work for it, the ECB will go for that," said Joanne Collins, senior economist at Daiwa SBCM in London. \par \par \uc2  "The ECB would be more inclined to use the interest rate instrument before dirtying its hands with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  The BOJ has now \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  and sold yen at least 15 times since June 1999. It has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at least once via the ECB but the ECB has never \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on its own behalf in the course of the euro's short life. \par \par \uc2  Wariness that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be unsuccessful and further weaken the ECB's already battered credibility, coupled with the view that monetary policy is a more effective tool in strengthening a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , were likely to make the ECB reluctant to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Collins said she expected the ECB to raise interest rates by 25 basis points next week, after the euro-zone's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left rates steady last week but expressed concern about the inflationary risks of a weak euro. \par \par \uc2  JAPAN GDP SEEN NEGATIVE \par \par \uc2  The euro could also find support against the yen without \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  help if Japanese gross domestic product data out on Monday is weak enough, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Kirit Shah, chief strategist at Sanwa in London, said only a more drastic fall in the euro against dollar and yen was likely to goad the ECB into action, Shah said. \par \par \uc2  "If the euro falls below $0.90, the ECB will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. "If they raise by 50 basis points and also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , that could take the euro back to parity and I will be revising my forecasts." \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro fell to a record low just below $0.94\tab   last week and is currently perched only a cent and a half away from these troughs.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro has fallen as much as 15 percent against the U.S. dollar since its launch in January, 1999, losing out to the relative appeal of the U.S. economy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par With euro/yen weakness seen driven more by broad weakness in the single \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  than independent yen strength, Japan would have limited power to turn euro/yen around on its own, said Derek Halpenny, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  economist at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi in London.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He said this could explain the modest size of its latest \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which traders estimated at $1.0 billion.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The Japanese authorities think there is very little they can do when the potential for futher euro declines against the dollar are very significant," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((London Capital Markets +44 171 542 6320, carolyn.cohn@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw3804qwf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
