\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen falls across the board with BoJ  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Genevieve Wilkinson \par \uc2 579 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 23:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, March 8 (Reuters) - The yen fell against the euro and dollar on Wednesday after Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold its own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help break the yen's quick pace of recent gains. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan surprised the market overnight, buying dollars for yen for the second time this year. \par \par \uc2  Ordered by Tokyo's Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa, the move was aimed at soothing the yen's rapid ascent brought on in part with a sudden crush to repatriate funds ahead of the end of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's financial year on March 31. \par \par \uc2  With the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , authorities drove the yen as low as 107.45 yen per dollar and 103.19 yen to the euro. \par \par \uc2  Although the yen had pared some of its losses by the end of New York trading it remained down more than a full percent against both the dollar and the yen amid ongoing nervousness that there may be more \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action ahead. \par \par \uc2  "I would think this \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not a one-off thing," said Seth Garrett, global head of spot trading at Credit Suisse First Boston. \par \par \uc2  Japanese officials have feared that a sharp rise in the yen may choke off the nation's fragile economic recovery. Yet hopes that recovery may pick up speed soon has contributed to reasons to buy Japanese assets and the yen. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile the euro also gained some ground against the dollar, raising itself off a week low at 95.24 cents to stand 0.10 percent higher against the dollar at 96.05 cents in late New York trading. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said investors had taken profits and remained worried by the prospects for U.S. equities. \par \par \uc2  Even though the Dow Jones industrial average and technology heavy Nasdaq composite index both bounced back on Wednesday, their sharp losses on Tuesday still worried the market. \par \par \uc2  European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Vice President Christian Noyer helped the euro a touch by saying the 11-nation's growth rate could top 3 percent this year, which is above many analysts' 2.5 percent growth rates. \par \par \uc2  However analysts remained concerned about the euro's general health because it failed to gain significant momentum when Germany's unemployment rate fell for the fifth consecutive month. Instead traders focused on less positive news showing that German manufacturing was weaker than expected in January. \par \par \uc2  For now some dealers expect the euro will trade sideways but some analysts said a fall to 92 cents, which would mark fresh life lows, is possible. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 2141GMT.  All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at \par \par \uc2  2130GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab    Last     US Close  %Chg   YTD %  1999\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Cls\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab 07 Mar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/dlr\tab \tab    0.9606   0.9596   +0.10   -4.61   1.0070\par Dlr/yen\tab \tab     107.12   106.07   +0.99   +4.80   102.21\par Euro/yen\tab \tab    102.92   101.77   +1.13   -0.17   103.10\par Dlr/swiss\tab \tab   1.6720   1.6744   -0.14   +5.14   1.5902\par Stg/dlr\tab \tab     1.5807   1.5793   +0.09   -2.28   1