\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro transfixed ahead of U.S. jobs data. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Lisa Jucca \par \uc2 660 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 14:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, March 3 (Reuters) - The euro was paralysed against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday, unable to break free from its current tight ranges ahead of key U.S. jobs data at 1330 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said dealers were wary of betting too hard in either direction amid uncertainties over the reaction of U.S. assets markets to the jobs figures. \par \par \uc2  Economists expect on average U.S. February jobless rate to be unchanged at 4.0 percent. They also estimate 206,000 new jobs were created in February outside the farm sector. Average early earnings are seen rising by 0.3 percent. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said only stronger-than-expected data could propel the euro above its Friday's $0.9615-75 range against the dollar, as the report would rekindle fears of an aggressive U.S. Federal Reserve tightening to stop inflation. \par \par \uc2  "The euro has so far managed to hold around $0.9650, but I do not see much potential in either way as dealers are awaiting today's U.S. payroll figures," said Klaus Kusber, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Dresdner Kleinwort Benson in Frankfurt. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers will be looking at how U.S. equities will react to the data. The risk for the euro is on the upside, but only if we see very strong U.S. figures." \par \par \uc2  Earlier in the session stronger-than-expected increases in January Italian producer prices briefly boosted the euro to the top of its day's range. The data showed the monthly gain was the biggest since May 1995 and the annual increase the largest in nearly four years. \par \par \uc2  But its impact was countered by German and Italian services purchasing managers indices which pointed to a slowdown in activity in the sector in February. \par \par \uc2  Dealers ignored a broadly steady euro zone services survey. \par \par \uc2  "Euro/dollar is almost paralysed. The services surveys we got this morning did not move the market that much as the market is already concentrating on the U.S. non-farm payroll data due later today," said Fabio Fraschetti, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Banca Nazionale del Lavoro in London. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the sentiment for the euro remained bearish and it was unlikely to make much headway in the short-term after the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept rates unchanged on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  But they added relatively hawkish remarks by ECB President Wim Duisenberg at a news briefing on Thursday would prevent the euro to fall much below current levels. \par \par \uc2  "We had some decent robust data this week and the comments from Duisenberg yesterday were very hawkish," said Joanne Collins, senior economist at Daiwa SBCM Europe in London. "The ECB is obviously watching the euro and is certainly concerned about it to the point where people are starting to worry that when it (the ECB) does move, they might do 50 and not 25. That talk is certainly providing some support to the euro." \par \par \uc2  Duisenberg said on Thursday that the ECB was strongly interested in a strong euro and that a firm \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in the interest of Europe. \par \par \uc2  YEN SIDELINED AHEAD OF DATA \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile the euro was holding ground above 104 yen, one yen above Thursday's one-month lows just above 103 yen. \par \par \uc2  Wariness about potential \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on euro/yen by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the wake of the yen's recent gains across the board was keeping the euro propped against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But the yen was generally sidelined in view of the U.S. economic reports, they added. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was holding within a quarter yen of day's highs at 108 yen it hit after Japanese Economic Planning Minister Taichi Sakaiya said earlier an economic recovery was just around the corner. Option-related buying was keeping the dollar propped well above its Wednesday's one-month lows around 106.50. \par \par \uc2  ((Lisa Jucca, London Capital Markets 0171 542 6745, elisabetta.jucca@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw3305vbv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
