\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro capped below $0.97, awaits U.S. data. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Lisa Jucca \par \uc2 646 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 12:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, March 3 (Reuters) - The euro was caged in a narrow range below $0.97 on Friday with dealers wary of pushing it too far in either direction ahead of key U.S. jobs data at 1330 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Mixed economic reports from the euro zone earlier in the day gave little guidance to traders as signs of a slowdown in the pace of expansion in the Italian and German service sectors offset the strength of Italian producer price data. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the momentum for the euro remained neagative as dealers feared U.S. jobs data would show the U.S. labour market was tight but not producing inflationary pressures, bringing relief to U.S. assets markets and helping the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "Euro/dollar is almost paralysed. The services surveys we got this morning did not move the market that much as the market is already concentrating on the U.S. non-farm payroll data due later today," said Fabio Fraschetti, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Banca Nazionale del Lavoro in London. \par \par \uc2  "The U.S. data should create the condition for a stable equity market. The data should favour the treasury markets as well. On the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a positive performance of both markets should help the dollar continue to appreciate against the euro." \par \par \uc2  Earlier in the session stronger-than-expected increases in January Italian producer prices briefly boosted the euro to the top of its Friday's range towards $0.98. The data showed the monthly gain was the biggest since May 1995 and the annual increase the largest in nearly four years. \par \par \uc2  But its impact was countered by German and Italian services purchasing managers indices which pointed to a slowdown in activity in the sector in February. \par \par \uc2  Dealers ignored a broadly steady euro zone services survey. By 1050 GMT the euro was trading in the middle of a its range around $0.9650/60. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the sentiment for the euro remained bearish and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unlikely to make much headway after the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its interest rates unchanged on Thursday, crushing hopes of a morale-boosting hike for the struggling \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  LINGERING BOJ FEARS KEEP YEN CURBED \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro rebounded after falling within sights of Thursday's lows around 103 yen in Asia, supported by wariness about the potential for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on euro/yen by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the wake of the yen's recent gains across the board. \par \par \uc2  "The euro looks vulnerable, but the market is worried about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after overnight talk that the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy euros against the yen in Europe (on Thursday), although most people dismissed it as a rumour," said a dealer at a trust bank in Tokyo. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  worries are likely to increase if the euro dips below 103 yen to approach its all-time low near 102 yen set on December 6 last year, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Speculation that Deutsche Telekom AG may bid $80 billion for U.S. Qwest Communications International Inc supported the dollar against the euro in Asian trade, as it implied a more direct investment outflow into the United States from Europe. \par \par \uc2  Deutsche Telekom said on Thursday it had no comment on a Wall Street Journal report saying it was in merger talks with Qwest. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lost steam against the dollar after a bouyant climb this weak on the back of fund repatriation before the end of the fiscal year in Japan in March. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was pegged within half a yen range of day's highs at 108 JPY=) it hit after Japanese Economic Planning Minister Taichi Sakaiya said earlier an economic recovery was just around the corner. Option-related buying was keeping the dollar propped well above its Wednesday's one-month lows around 106.50. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw3305t9o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
