\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Little respite for weary euro, US data eyed. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Kanta Watanabe \par \uc2 766 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 08:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, March 3 (Reuters) - The euro remained under pressure in Tokyo on Friday after the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its interest rates unchanged overnight, crushing hopes of a morale-boosting hike for the struggling \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  may extend its losses if U.S. February employment data due at 1330 GMT provides fresh signs of the relative strength of the U.S. economy and boosts the dollar. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In late afternoon trade, the euro was quoted at $0.9664/69\tab  , compared with $0.9642 in New York late on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par It briefly dipped as low as $0.9600 in mid-afternoon, but found support on buying by overseas players aiming to protect options positions with strike prices below that level.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Another factor supporting the euro was wariness about the potential for euro-buying, yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the wake of the yen's recent rise versus the euro. Against the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the euro was at 103.94/04 yen\tab     , up from 103.75 yen in New York late on Thursday and Friday's Tokyo intraday low of around 103.24 yen.\par The dollar was quoted at 107.63/68 yen\tab  , steady from 107.73 yen in New York late on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The euro looks vulnerable, but the market is worried about \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after overnight talk that the BOJ \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to buy euros against the yen in Europe (on Thursday), although most people dismissed it as a rumour," said a dealer at a trust bank.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  worries are likely to increase if the euro dips below 103 yen to approach its all-time low near 102 yen set on December 6 last year, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The euro's drop versus the yen is putting indirect downward pressure on the dollar against the yen. But a lot of people were sidelined before the U.S. job data release tonight," the trust bank dealer said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Economists polled by Reuters forecast, on average, a 206,000 increase in U.S. non-farm payrolls in February after a strong 387,000 rise in January.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The unemployment rate is expected to hold steady at 4.0 percent. The data will be released at 1330 GMT Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "If the jobless rate dips below 4.0 percent, I think that could have a strong psychological impact on the market by heralding the strength of the U.S. economy," said a dealer at a city bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Speculation that Deutsche Telekom AG may bid $80 billion for U.S. Qwest Communications International Inc also gave the dollar support against the euro, as it implied a more direct investment outflow into the United States from Europe.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Deutsche Telekom said on Thursday it had no comment on a Wall Street Journal report saying it was in merger talks with Qwest.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Early on Friday, the dollar briefly rose as high as 108.08 yen on pre-weekend short-covering by dealers.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But the dollar quickly slipped back below 108 yen on comments by Japanese Economic Planning Minister Taichi Sakaiya saying that an economic recovery was right around the corner.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Sakaiya said consumption-related indicators in January showed a "considerably clear" economic recovery, adding that private consumption had hit bottom in the last three months of 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He added that gross domestic product figures for the fourth quarter would be released in the next two weeks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A Reuters poll of 19 Economists this week produced a median forecast of a 1.1 percent drop in the October-December GDP from the previous quarter. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-3432-9780 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 0703 GMT.  All data taken from Reuters\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab      Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   1999 Cls\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   02 Mar.\par \tab \tab \tab      -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr\tab \tab     0.9660   0.9642   +0.19    -4.07   1.0070\par  Dlr/yen\tab \tab      107.65   107.73   -0.07    +5.32   102.21\par  Euro/yen\tab \tab     103.95   103.75   +0.19    +0.82   103.10\par  Dlr/swiss\tab \tab    1.6619   1.6629   -0.06    +4.51   1.5902\par  Stg/dlr\tab \tab      1.5786   1.5759   +0.17    -2.41   1.6176\par  Can/dlr\tab \tab      1.4555   1.4557   -0.01    +0.69   1.4455\par  Aus/dlr\tab \tab      0.6095   0.6064   +0.51    -7.13   0.6563\par  Euro/swiss\tab \tab   1.6059   1.6061   -0.01    +0.14   1.6036\par  Euro/stg\tab \tab     0.6118   0.6118   +0.00    -1.94   0.6239.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw3305ssf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
