\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro sluggish, supportive remarks help yen. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Ayumi Moriyama \par \uc2 715 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 04:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, March 3 (Reuters) - The euro was vulnerable in late morning trade on Friday after the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) refrained from raising rates, while the yen was boosted after officials made upbeat remarks about Japan's economic prospects. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said activity was relatively subdued as the market wound down after a hectic week and ahead of the release of key U.S. employment report for February due at 1330 GMT. \par \par \uc2  The European single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was hovering around $0.9645/50 after surviving a test of $0.9620, compared with $0.9642 at the overnight New York close. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Against the yen, the euro stood at 103.67/74\tab     , from 103.75 yen in late U.S. trade, with the market wary about possible euro-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (BOJ) if the 14-month old \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  falls to historical lows near 102.00 yen.\par The dollar was quoted at 107.44/52 yen\tab   after short-covering led it above 108 yen earlier in the day, compared with 107.73 yen in late New York.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Traders said the quick recovery of the yen was triggered by comments by Japanese officials that an economic recovery was right around the corner.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "(Economic Planning Minister Taichi) Sakaiya's comment indicating a clear recovery in the economy sent the dollar down to the 107-yen level," said one Japanese city bank dealer.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Sakaiya said consumption-related indicators in January showed a "considerably clear" economic recovery, adding that private consumption had hit bottom in the last three months of 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "During the October-December quarter, production improved while private demand remained sluggish, but consumption turned towards improvment in January," he told reporters.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Gross domestic product figures for the fourth quarter would be released in the next two weeks, he added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Sakaiya's bullish tone was followed by Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa's remarks that he expected corporate capital spending to start rising around September.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He told the Upper House that personal consumption, the largest component and one of the most sluggish portions of the economy, would likely "improve from the January-March quarter to the April-June quarter".\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro, which sagged as far as $0.9615 in New York following the ECB's decision not to raise rates, remained under pressure even after ECB President Wim Duisenberg said a strong euro was in Europe's interests.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The euro's bearishness wil remain so for some time," said Yasuharu Tsuru, manager of the international treasury division at Mitsubishi Trust & Banking.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He said the chances of the ECB \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were slim, but added that the weakness of the euro against the yen raised the possibility that that could shift across to affect the dollar's level against the yen as well.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The single \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was also under pressure from speculation that Deutsche Telekom AG  may bid $80 billion for U.S. Qwest Communiations International Inc , implying the need to buy dollars.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The focus was now on U.S. February payrolls figures, with many market players expecting unemployment to fall to a new cyclical low of 3.9 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In January, the jobless rate fell to a 30-year low of 4.0 percent, and new employment payrolls rose to 387,000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-3432-8550 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 0309 GMT.  All data taken from Reuters\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab      Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   1999 Cls\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   02 Mar.\par \tab \tab \tab      -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr\tab \tab     0.9640   0.9642   -0.02    -4.27   1.0070\par  Dlr/yen\tab \tab      107.40   107.73   -0.31    +5.08   102.21\par  Euro/yen\tab \tab     103.63   103.75   -0.12    +0.51   103.10\par  Dlr/swiss\tab \tab    1.6659   1.6629   +0.18    +4.76   1.5902\par  Stg/dlr\tab \tab      1.5770   1.5759   +0.07    -2.51   1.6176\par  Can/dlr\tab \tab      1.4561   1.4557   +0.03    +0.73   1.4455\par  Aus/dlr\tab \tab      0.6095   0.6064   +0.51    -7.13   0.6563\par  Euro/swiss\tab \tab   1.6061   1.6061   +0.00    +0.16   1.6036\par  Euro/stg\tab \tab     0.6113   0.6118   -0.08    -2.02   0.6239.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw3305s1e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
