\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  - Euro trapped as data gives mixed signals. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sabrina Ghani \par \uc2 619 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 09:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, March 3 (Reuters) - The euro was broadly steady on Friday as signs of a slowdown in the pace of expansion in the Italian and German service sectors offset the strength of Italian producer price data. \par \par \uc2  Stronger-than-expected increases in Italian producer prices bolstered the euro, with the monthly gain the biggest since May 1995 and the annual increase the largest in nearly four years. \par \par \uc2  But its impact was countered by German and Italian services purchasing managers indices which pointed to a slowdown in activity in the sector. Euro zone PMI is out at 0900 GMT. \par \par \uc2  The euro was therefore expected to remain within the ranges of the past two days before the release of key U.S. February jobs data at 1330 GMT. \par \par \uc2  "The EMU PMI services data is due later and we expect the indices to be ticking up. If anything they will be euro supportive, but I doubt it if alone it could push the euro above $0.9750," said Mike Moran, treasury economist at Standard Chartered Bank in London. \par \par \uc2  "I see the euro trading water today but we could see U.S. induced movement. We expect slightly tighter U.S. payroll figures which could pull the dollar back a little bit." \par \par \uc2  BOJ WORRIES SUPPORT EURO/YEN \par \par \uc2  The euro pegged nearly half a cent below $0.97. \par \par \uc2  It briefly dipped near $0.9600 in the Tokyo session, but found support on buying by overseas players aiming to protect options positions with strike prices below that level. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro rebounded after falling within sights of Thursday's lows around 103 yen, supported by lingering wariness about the potential for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on euro/yen by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the wake of the yen's recent rally across the board. \par \par \uc2  "The euro looks vulnerable, but the market is worried about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after overnight talk that the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy euros against the yen in Europe (on Thursday), although most people dismissed it as a rumour," said a dealer at a trust bank. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  worries are likely to increase if the euro dips below 103 yen to approach its all-time low near 102 yen set on December 6 last year, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The euro's drop versus the yen is putting indirect downward pressure on the dollar against the yen. But a lot of people were sidelined before the U.S. job data release tonight," the trust bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Traders, meanwhile said the sentiment for the euro remained bearish and it was unlikely to make much headway after the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its interest rates unchanged on Thursday, crushing hopes of a morale-boosting hike for the struggling \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Speculation that Deutsche Telekom AG may bid $80 billion for U.S. Qwest Communications International Inc supported the dollar against the euro, as it implied a more direct investment outflow into the United States from Europe. \par \par \uc2  Deutsche Telekom said on Thursday it had no comment on a Wall Street Journal report saying it was in merger talks with Qwest. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lost steam after a bouyant climb this weak on the back of fund repatriation before the end of the fiscal year in Japan in March. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was pegged within half a yen range of day's highs at 107.69, down from the day's high around 108 yen after Japanese Economic Planning Minister Taichi Sakaiya said an economic recovery was right around the corner. \par \par \uc2  Sakaiya said consumption-related indicators in January showed a "considerably clear" economic recovery, adding that private consumption had hit bottom in the last three months of 1999. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw33057l8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
