\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ conducted no  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\uc2  in Feb-bankers. \b0\par\par\uc2 289 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Februar 2000\par 11:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Feb 29 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) conducted no dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in February, after spending more than $5 billion in January to curtail the yen's strength, bankers in Tokyo said on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Data released on Tuesday by the BOJ showed that Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) received 10 billion yen from the private sector in February through its special \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account. \par \par \uc2  Net fund outflows from MOF, in the form of payments from the special account to the private sector, are often viewed as evidence of yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which the MOF conducts through the BOJ. \par \par \uc2  But the net fund inflow into the special \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account in February meant that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell yen this month, bankers said. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ data included the last two trading days of the previous month, but not the last two business days of this month, as \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  settlements are made two days after transactions. \par \par \uc2  In January, the MOF paid 575 billion yen to the private sector through the special \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account, which bankers said was an indication that the BOJ had spent about $5.62 billion to support the dollar against the yen in the first month of this year. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ was last detected conducting yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on January 4. The MOF has confirmed that it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  through the BOJ on that day to buy dollars for yen. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ acts as an agent for the MOF and conducts actual dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  through transactions with brokers and private banks. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-3432-9780 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw2t069ij\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
