\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2  can be successful - ECB study. \b0\par\par\uc2 368 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Februar 2000\par 17:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Feb 23 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the foreign exchanges can successfully influence exchange rates, particularly when authorities act in concert and relatively infrequently, a European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  working paper said. \par \par \uc2  The paper, entitled "On the Effectiveness of Sterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ", said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to be of limited use on its own as a policy instrument for achieving long-term effects on exchange rates. \par \par \uc2  However, it said it had found \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be more effective in the short term than previous studies had suggested. \par \par \uc2  "The results clearly suggested that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is indeed effective in terms of influencing the evolution of exchange rates over the short run," said the working paper which was first released on February 14. \par \par \uc2  The ECB working paper used official \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  data provided by the Bundesbank and Federal Reserve to assess the impact of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the dollar/mark exchange rate since the Plaza Agreement of 1985. \par \par \uc2  The effectiveness of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in either slowing a trend or in reversing it was found to increase if central banks coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The findings emphasize the importance of coordinated and relatively infrequent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , suggesting that a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could in fact improve the likelihood of observing a success by conducting its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a certain manner," \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on at least 14 occasions between June 1999 and January in a bid to curb yen strength, including once via the Federal Reserve and once through the ECB. During that time the yen rose as much as 19 percent against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  However, central banks from the major industrial nations have not been spotted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in concert since 1998. The ECB itself has only been detected in the market when it was acting on behalf of the Bank of Japan in June 1999. \par \par \uc2  The paper said there was also some evidence to suggest that small-scale \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  were less likely to be successful. \par \par \uc2  An ECB official said the contents of the working paper did not necessarily reflect the views of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  ((Swaha Pattanaik, London Capital Markets, +44 171 542 6284, swaha.pattanaik@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw2n06pd5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
