\par\par \b \uc2  Japan FB ceiling raised for flexibility on  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - MOF. \b0\par\par\uc2 243 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Februar 2000\par 09:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Feb 1 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to lift a ceiling on issuance of financing bills (FBs) was intended to allow a flexible response as needed to further rises in the yen, a ministry official said on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The ministry said on Monday the ceiling on the issuance of FBs, used to fund \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , would be lifted to 59 trillion yen in the fiscal year beginning on April 1 from 49 trillion yen at present. \par \par \uc2  Asked at a briefing on Tuesday what the ministry's intentions were in the move, a MOF official said: "Since the yen might appreciate further, we wanted room to be able to act flexibly." \par \par \uc2  The ministry, acting through the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets last year and most recently stepped into the market on January 4. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese government fears that the appreciation of the yen since last summer may choke off the country's fledgling economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  The official, briefing reporters after Tuesday's release of foreign reserves data for January, added: "We have reviewed the FB issuance ceiling in the past and have raised it when necessary." \par \par \uc2  The ceiling has been steadily raised in recent years, he said, noting it was at 28 trillion yen in the government's 1994/95 budget. ((Tokyo newsroom +81-3 3432 8022 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument 