\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Japan frets over yen, to keep policy on hold. \b0\par\par\uc2  By William Mallard \par \uc2 556 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Januar 2000\par 09:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Jan 31 (Reuters) - Japan's government and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  vowed again on Monday to keep supporting the fragile economy, saying the level of the yen is a threat to recovery despite its recent fall against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Finance Ministry beefed up its arsenal for combating the yen's strength through market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would continue driving short-term interest rates to near zero while watching out for adverse effects from the strong yen. \par \par \uc2  Despite a jump by the dollar on Friday to more than three-month highs against the yen, the still-strong Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflames deflationary pressures and erodes the yen value of Japanese companies' overseas earnings. \par \par \uc2  MOF THINKS YEN TOO STRONG, BOJ VIGILANT \par \par \uc2  "There is no change in our view that an excessive yen appreciation is unfavourable for economic recovery," said top finance bureaucrat Nobuaki Usui. \par \par \uc2  The ministry proposed raising the ceiling on the issuance of bills used for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by 10 trillion yen ($93.63 billion) in the coming fiscal year to 59 trillion yen. \par \par \uc2  Japan won a statement of renewed concern from its Group of Seven partners at a January 22 meeting about the possible effect of the yen's rise on the Japanese and world economies. \par \par \uc2  In return, the BOJ had to promise anew that it will keep interest rates at zero - where they have been for almost a year - to support the economy's crawl out of its worst postwar downturn. \par \par \uc2  In the Osaka area, home to many large exporters, firms are strongly concerned about the yen's trajectory although many firms expect higher profits in the half year to March through cost cuts and strong overseas demand, said BOJ Osaka branch manager Minoru Masubuchi. \par \par \uc2  The dollar surged more than one yen in New York on Friday and held on much of its gains in the Tokyo session. It was trading around 106.75 yen at 5:30 p.m. (0830 GMT) \par \par \uc2  MONETARY, FISCAL POLICY ON HOLD \par \par \uc2  BOJ Governor Masaru Hayami, reiterating that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's zero interest rate policy is on hold for now, told the bank's branch managers a careful watch was needed on the effects of the high yen since last summer on the economy and prices. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said it will maintain its zero rate policy until deflation fears subside. \par \par \uc2  "It is appropriate for the BOJ to maintain its zero interest-rate policy, since Japan's economy has not reached a situation in which deflationary concerns have been dispelled," Hayami said. \par \par \uc2  Hayami is stuck between his desire to nudge rates up a bit as soon as conditions warrant and government pressure to maintain, or even loosen, monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  On fiscal policy, Prime Minister Keizo Obuchi reiterated to parliament that the economy is improving but remains weak, vowing not to let up on government spending until recovery is firmly in place. \par \par \uc2  Data released on Monday showed the economy's continued dependence on government largesse. Orders received by 50 major construction companies slumped 13.1 percent in December from a year earlier, with public-sector orders plunging 32 percent, the Construction Ministry said. ((Tatsuo Ito, Tokyo newsroom +81-3 3432-8022 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par