\par\par \b \uc2  MOF to up  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2  funds 10 trln yen-JIJI. \b0\par\par\uc2 176 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Januar 2000\par 13:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Jan 28 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  is boosting its funds for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by 10 trillion yen in order to halt the yen's export-crippling rise, JIJI Press news agency, monitored here, reported on Friday. \par \par \uc2  A draft budget for fiscal 2000/01 submitted to parliament on Friday contained a plan to raise the ceiling for issuance of short-term bills the ministry uses to fund \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Jiji said. \par \par \uc2  "(It is) in order to cope with movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market with greater margin," Jiji quoted an official at the ministry's international finance bureau as saying. \par \par \uc2  The ceiling was to be raised by 10 trillion to a total of 59 trillion. It had been raised by 10 trillion in the second extra budget for the current fiscal year ending March 31 which had been passed last month, Jiji added. ((Shin Kishima, London Capital Markets +44-171-542-6721, shinichi.kishima@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw1s05544\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
