\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Buoyant dollar soars across the board. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Lida Poletz \par \uc2 921 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Januar 2000\par 20:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Jan 28 (Reuters) - The dollar hurtled higher against all other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in unusually volatile trade on Friday, hitting record peaks against Europe's embattled \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and touching 3-1/2 month highs against the yen. \par \par \uc2  The euro, damaged by scepticism about Europe's economic outlook and apparent lack of concern from European officials, extended overnight declines to hit a record low of 97.36 cents, down 1-1/2 cents on the day. \par \par \uc2  Other European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  tumbled in the euro's wake. The Swiss franc sinking to 10-year lows above 1.65 francs per dollar and the British pound tumbled to its lowest level against the greenback in nearly a month. \par \par \uc2  But to the surprise of many in the market, the dollar also launched a dizzying rally against the Japanese yen - hitting 107.26 yen, a gain of two full yen from the previous close. \par \par \uc2  And the Australian dollar and New Zealand dollar, often called commodity \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , plunged to their lowest levels in months. \par \par \uc2  "It's become a dollar story, and it's a very neat story because you're seeing the dollar performing in a rare way," said Craig Larimer, market strategist at BancOne. "There's a very uniform pattern against all \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including commodity \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and industrialised \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  Most market player expressed bewilderment as to why the dollar had risen so sharply across the board. \par \par \uc2  "Traders were scratching their heads as to why all of a sudden everyone was bailing out of everything against the dollar," said Mark Thome, vice president at Fortis. \par \par \uc2  "People haven't really thought of the dollar as the strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the lineup and suddenly it's acting like it is." \par \par \uc2  A report released at the start of U.S. trade showed much stronger-than-expected inventory building and consumers' voracious appetite for new goods allowed the U.S. economy to grow at a surprisingly strong 5.8 percent annual rate during the last quarter of 1999. \par \par \uc2  And the employment cost index, reportedly a favoured indicator of Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan, jumped 1.1 percent in the fourth quarter, all but ensuring the Federal Reserve will raise interest rates next week. \par \par \uc2  "These numbers are bound to help the dollar," Sanwa Bank senior trader Jeffrey Yu said. \par \par \uc2  But improving data in the euro zone, including a drop in French unemployment in December to 10.6 percent on Friday, were not enough to lure investors away from the relative attractions of America's red-hot economy and resilient stock market. \par \par \uc2  Other U.S. markets were mixed and equally choppy after the data. U.S. stock tumbled sharply, with the Dow trading down more than 150 points in the early U.S. afternoon. But money from slumping stocks was redirected into U.S. Treasuries, which launched a stunning rebound from early data-driven lows. \par \par \uc2  The euro's steep decline brought the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to more than 16 percent below the level at which it was launched with champagne celebrations in January 1999. Traders said there was no reason to believe it would not fall further, perhaps to 95 cents. \par \par \uc2  In addition to economic concerns, the euro was suffering from a range of political issues undermining the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's credibility, analysts and dealers said. \par \par \uc2  These included lack of structural reform in euro-zone economies, the financial scandal surrounding former German chancellor and euro architect Helmut Kohl which has threatened to embroil France, and the possibility of the far-right Freedom Party joining the Austrian government. \par \par \uc2  By contrast, the yen has exhibited persistent strength against the dollar as investors bet on signs of improvement in the Japanese economy and a buoyant Tokyo stocks. \par \par \uc2  In fact \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly to tame yen strength in recent months, fearing a too-strong yen will hurt economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  But traders ruled out \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a possible factor in the dollar's surge against the yen on Friday, linking the rapid upmove to technical buying. \par \par \uc2  "The real thing behind it is there was a technical break-out above the November double top above 106.60, when in shot to 107," said analyst Andrew Chavariat of Banque Paribas. And now there's no real resistance until the 108 area." \par \par \uc2  ((U.S. Financial Markets Desk 212 859 1868)). \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 1907GMT.  All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. \par \par \uc2  close at 2130GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab    Last     US Close  %Chg   YTD %  1999\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Cls\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab 27 Jan.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/dlr\tab \tab    0.9752   0.9881   -1.31   -3.16   1.0070\par Dlr/yen\tab \tab     106.91   1