\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro hits record lows, verbal support limp. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 787 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Januar 2000\par 14:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Jan 28 (Reuters) - The euro tumbled to record lows, nearly two cents below dollar parity on Friday, driven by European officials' apparent indifference to its plight. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Concern about the relative growth and political outlook in the euro zone in comparison with the United States also weighed on the single \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which fell as low as $0.9830\tab  , its third record low this week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  This was more than 16 percent below the level at which it was launched with champagne celebrations in January 1999, and equivalent to the once-mighty German mark's lowest levels against the dollar in more than 10 years. \par \par \uc2  "Investment flows will continue to go against the euro, and I can see it going down to $0.90 over the next year," said Stephen Lewis, chief economist at Monument Derivatives in London. \par \par \uc2  Traders said there was no sign the euro's downward momentum was waning and that it could be headed in the short term toward $0.9779, equivalent to 2.00 marks in dollar/mark terms, and then on to $0.95. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said improving data in the euro zone, most recently Friday's figures showing a drop in French unemployment in December to 10.6 percent, were not enough to lure investors away from the relative attractions of resilient U.S. stock markets, which appear braced for a U.S. rate rise next week. \par \par \uc2  "We've heard all the current account deficit arguments over the past three to four years why the dollar is overvalued, but my watch has stopped, waiting for them to take effect," said Cameron Crise, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Warburg Dillon Read in London. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said in addition to economic concerns, the euro was suffering from a range of political issues undermining the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's credibility. \par \par \uc2  These included lack of structural reform in euro-zone economies, the financial scandal surrounding former German chancellor and euro architect Helmut Kohl, which has threatened to embroil France, and the possibility of the far-right Freedom Party joining the Austrian government. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  WARINESS WANES \par \par \uc2  Traders said the euro's decline accelerated this week after finance ministers of the Group of Seven industrial powers made no mention of its weakness in a communique issued after a meeting in Japan last Saturday. \par \par \uc2  They said European officials' remarks also appeared lacklustre in the face of the falls, disappointing traders who had hoped for verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the sidelines of this week's World Economic Forum in Davos, Switzerland. \par \par \uc2  Bundesbank President Ernst Welteke said in Davos the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not neglect exchange rate developments, as they were a key element of the bank's two-pillar strategy. \par \par \uc2  But traders said the infant European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had yet to instill the kind of fear in the market that the U.S. Federal Reserve and other central banks have over the years with aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Traders said fear of such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the euro's behalf was watered down after ECB Chief Economist Otmar Issing said earlier this week there were no euro exchange levels at which it would be automatically triggered. \par \par \uc2  However, if the fourth quarter U.S. gross domestic product and employment cost index due out at 1330 GMT showed signs of overheating in the U.S. economy and hit Wall Street stocks, the euro could find some short-term relief, traders said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro also came within a whisker of Thursday's 60.22-pence record low against the British pound\tab      on Friday, equivalent to 3.24 marks in sterling/mark terms, the single \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's own woes compounded by expectations for higher British interest rates.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But it pulled back from earlier three-week lows around 103 yen , amid broad yen gains following a news report hinting at the possibility of Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb the yen's export-crippling strength.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Japanese news agency Jiji said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was building up funds by 10 trillion yen for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Joint \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  between the BOJ and the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to cap the yen and support the euro was likely to be more effective than unilateral \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , analysts said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The BOJ has already \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at least 14 times since last June to put a lid on the yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar rallied above 105 yen\tab   from one-week lows against the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on the back of the Jiji report.\par The friendless euro, meanwhile, also dragged the Swiss franc lower in its wake, pushing the franc\tab   to 10-year lows near 1.64 to the dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((London Capital Markets +44 171 542 6320, carolyn.cohn@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw1s04w02\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
