\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro eyes parity vs dollar, Dow seen as key. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sabrina Ghani \par \uc2 489 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Januar 2000\par 12:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Jan 25 (Reuters) - The euro fell to within half a cent of parity against the dollar on Tuesday, shedding earlier gains as a rise in S&P futures fanned expectations that U.S. stocks would stage a recovery later in the day. \par \par \uc2  The euro had rallied as far as $1.0096 in Asia, buoyed by Monday's 2.16 percent fall in the Dow Jones Industrial Average. However the dollar clawed back ground as traders focused on a rise in S&P futures. \par \par \uc2  "You should get a bounce back in Dow - March S&P futures are up about seven points - so the foundation for the dollar looks good," said Claudio Piron, treasury economist at Standard Chartered Bank. \par \par \uc2  "When it come to euro/dollar, the focus is on U.S. equities. You still have strong fundamentals with U.S. corporate earnings exceeding expectations and people typically buy (stocks) on dips, so you should get a bounce back up in Dow." \par \par \uc2  Euro/dollar was at trading $1.0040 by 1038 GMT compared with the seven-week lows around parity set on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said euro/dollar would now take its cue from how U.S. stock markets react to the testimony U.S. Federal Reserve Board Chairman Alan Greenspan is to deliver at 1500 GMT. \par \par \uc2  U.S. stocks were hit after Atlanta Fed President Jack Guynn, a voting Federal Open Market Committee member, said on Monday he did not see signs the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's three interest rate hikes in 1999 were slowing consumer demand. This reignited talk of an aggressive U.S. interest rate tightening. \par \par \uc2  Hawkish comments by Greenspan could rattle the stock markets further and give the euro some support against the dollar, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "If there is going to be continued concern about rising interest rates in the U.S., particularly as we hear Greenspan's comments later on, that might provide a bit of support for the euro," said Jeremy Stretch, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at NatWest Global Financial Markets in London. \par \par \uc2  YEN CAGED IN RANGES \par \par \uc2  The euro was also off its earlier high of 106.79 against the yen but remained 1.5 percent above Monday's three-week low at 104.80. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, The dollar was trapped in a tight range just below 106 yen. It was holding ground it gained on Monday after the Group of Seven nations at the weekend said they shared Japan's concern over the yen's strength. \par \par \uc2  The dollar/yen exchange rate showed limited reaction after Japanese Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to address disruptive movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, although no such movements had been seen so far on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, U.S. Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers said on Monday the U.S. savings rate was too low and called for Japan to target faster growth. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dw1p01bv2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
