\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro/dollar slips toward parity, Dow eyed. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sabrina Ghani \par \uc2 608 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Januar 2000\par 14:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Jan 25 (Reuters) - The euro slipped to within a quarter of a cent of parity on Tuesday, undermined by hopes that U.S. stocks would rebound later in the day. \par \par \uc2  The euro was down more than three quarters of a cent from the day's high of $1.0096 set in Asia on the back of Monday's 2.16 percent fall in the Dow Jones Industrials Average. \par \par \uc2  The euro started to descend in Europe with traders expecting the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to test parity for the second consecutive day as a 5.1 point rise in March S&P futures suggested a firmer opening for the Dow. \par \par \uc2  Euro/yen's one percent drop from day's high of 106.79 also weighed on the euro. \par \par \uc2  "The Dow came off on Monday but it did not support the euro because people think the Dow is going to rebound as the Federal Reserve is expected to keep inflation under control," said Matthew Clements, economist at Prebon Marshall Yamane in London. \par \par \uc2  "If the Dow went to 10,500 points, that would be a significant loss and should support the euro." \par \par \uc2  Euro failed to draw much support from a batch of euro-zone data showing that euro-zone economic recovery was on broadly on track. \par \par \uc2  Consumer prices in the German state of Hesse rose an annual 2.0 percent in January from 1.5 percent in December. In the state of North Rhine Westphalia CPI rose 1.9 percent from 1.4 percent in December, while Saxony's consumer prices rose 1.4 percent from 0.6 percent previously. \par \par \uc2  "There has been dramatic improvment in the euro zone data over the last six months. But the euro seems impervious to euro zone fundamentals. Until the Dow looses significantly or the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials' comments change in tone, I don't think the euro is going to go anywhere," said Clements at Prebon Marshall. \par \par \uc2  Euro/dollar was at $1.0015 by 1240 GMT compared with the seven-week lows around parity set on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said euro/dollar would now take its cue from how U.S. stock markets. Stocks were hit after Atlanta Fed President Jack Guynn, a voting Federal Open Market Committee member, said on Monday he did not see signs the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's three interest rate hikes in 1999 were slowing consumer demand. This reignited talk of an aggressive U.S. interest rate tightening. \par \par \uc2  "If there is going to be continued concern about rising interest rates in the U.S....that might provide a bit of support for the euro," said Jeremy Stretch, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at NatWest Global Financial Markets in London. \par \par \uc2  The market had been also awaiting U.S. Federal Reserve Alan Greenspan's testimony before the Senate budget committee, scheduled for later today. But the Senate committee cancelled the Fed chief's appearance due to a snowstorm that has hit Washington. \par \par \uc2  YEN IN FAMILIAR RANGES \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the yen was mired in familiar ranges against the euro and the dollar after the Group of Seven nations at the weekend said they shared Japan's concern over the yen's strength. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa said in Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to address disruptive movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, although no such movements had been seen so far on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  While the euro pulled back against the yen, it remained one percent above Monday's three-week low at 104.80. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen was pegged just below 106.00, but about one percent above Monday's lows of 104.62. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw1p0a789\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
