\par\par \b \uc2  Sakakibara says Japan policies key G7 topic - Jiji. \b0\par\par\uc2 295 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Januar 2000\par 08:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Jan 19 (Reuters) - Former Japanese Vice Finance Minister Eisuke Sakakibara said Japan's monetary policy will be one of the major issues discussed at a meeting of the Group of Seven (G7) nations' finance ministers and central bankers this weekend, Jiji news agency reported on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Sakakibara, who served as vice minister for international affairs until last July and whose comments often moved the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, said a soft landing for the U.S. economy and Japan's fiscal and monetary policies would be major topics at the meeting, Jiji reported. \par \par \uc2  Sakakibara was also quoted as saying it is too early for the Bank of Japan (BOJ) and the government to begin discussing the timing of a halt to the zero interest-rate policy or to reduce fiscal spending, as Japan's economy has not yet recovered. \par \par \uc2  "I think the G7 meeting will undoubtedly discuss \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policies, including \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, because that's what the market cares about," Sakakibara said. \par \par \uc2  Asked if he thinks Japan and the United States can establish a framework for joint \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Sakakibara said forming a cooperative relationship is of the utmost importance. \par \par \uc2  Regarding recent BOJ daily money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Sakakibara said he thinks the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should have left more liquidity in the market this week. \par \par \uc2  "I'm worried that there could be friction between Japan and the United States over the BOJ reducing the money market surplus too fast after increasing it late last year to cope with Y2K concerns," he told Jiji. \par \par \uc2  Sakakibara also said Japan should prevent the yen from rising beyond 100 yen to the dollar. ((Tokyo newsroom (813) 3432-8022 Tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw1j03dek\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
