\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro packs on gains as yen struggles. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Elizabeth Lazarowitz \par \uc2 766 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Januar 2000\par 19:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Jan 11 (Reuters) - Europe's single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  extended overnight gains in U.S. trading on Tuesday, boosted by worries about Wall Street's health and talk that global leaders may help Japan weaken the yen. \par \par \uc2  In early trading the euro hit a seven week high against the yen and stood more than one percent higher against it in early afternoon trading at 109.00 yen. The euro jumped more than a quarter of a cent against the dollar to trade over half a percent firmer at $1.0309. \par \par \uc2  Fresh interest in the euro emerged after it broke the psychologically significant 109 yen level, triggering some stop-loss buying. \par \par \uc2  "It certainly seems the crosses are the key influence of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets this morning," said Chris Davis, trader at Ruesch International. \par \par \uc2  The euro's gains against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped the dollar gain more ground against the yen, setting it in orbit around 106 yen, up more than three-quarters of a percent from Monday's closing level near 105 yen. \par \par \uc2  Lingering on traders minds have been worries that Japan could receive some support from global leaders in its efforts to trim the yen's strong gains which Japanese officials fear may choke off their country's economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  "Expectations are rising that there could be some discussion of concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and, if not, some comment regarding \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stance on weakening the yen," Davis said. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets last week, marking the 14th time the bank had sold yen on the open market since June 1999, hoping to curb the yen's industry-crippling rise. \par \par \uc2  Talk that Tokyo might try to enlist the help of G7 finance ministers and central bankers in taming the yen at their Jan. 22 meeting put the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  under broad-based pressure, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "It does look like Japanese yen buyers have backed away a bit ahead of the G7 meeting," Davis added. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said uncertainty about U.S. asset market performance had also helped lift the euro against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  In early U.S. afternoon trading the Dow Jones industrial average had pared its gains to stand 12 points higher at 11,583 while the technology-laden Nasdaq index fumbled in negative territory; the markets awaited a crush of earnings reports. \par \par \uc2  Wall Street had rallied since late last week and jumped Monday on news Internet provider AOL and media giant Time Warner Inc. plan to merge. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Europe's single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would likely continue to pin its hopes on less buoyant U.S. asset markets, but that it would likely run into technical resistance near its $1.0330 session high. \par \par \uc2  The euro had ticked slightly lower in late European trading after German engineering union IG Metall said on Tuesday its board recommended a pay raise of up to 5.5 percent for 2000. \par \par \uc2  Analysts called the pay demand excessive and said it might spark fresh fears of inflationary dangers, something \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders said helped dent the euro briefly. \par \par \uc2  "I think people will interpret that as putting potentially inflationary pressure inside the euro block," weighing on the euro, said Rick Gomes, managing director of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at HSBC in New York. \par \par \uc2      ((--U.S. Financial Markets Desk, 212-859-1607 )) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 1:26 p.m. (1826 GMT).  All data taken from \par \par \uc2  Reuters with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close \par \par \uc2  at 4:30 p.m. (2130 GMT). \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab    Last     US Close  %Chg   YTD %    1999\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab Jan. 10\tab \tab \tab  Close\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/dlr\tab \tab    1.0307   1.0253   +0.53   +2.35   1.0070\par Dlr/yen\tab \tab     105.80   105.10   +0.67   +3.51   102.21\par Euro/yen\tab \tab    109.08   107.80   +1.19   +5.80   103.10\par Dlr/swiss\tab \tab   1.5620   1.5680   -0.38   -1.77   1.5902\par Stg/dlr\tab \tab     1.6447   1.6365   +0.50   +1.68   1.6176\par Can/dlr\tab \tab     1.4562   1.4550   +0.08   +0.74   1.4455\par Aus/dlr\tab \tab     0.6573   0.6560   +0.20   +0.15   0.6563\par Euro/swiss\tab \tab  1.6104   1.6093   +0.07   +0.42   1.6036\par Euro/stg\tab \tab    0.6263   0.6260   +0.05   +0.38   0.6239\par  All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news ...\tab     Debt...   Indicators...\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports..\tab \tab \tab \tab \par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \par \par All spots\tab \par Tokyo spots\tab \par Europe spots\tab \par Volatilities\tab \par Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market info from BOJ\tab \par World \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Economic Forecasts...     Official rates...\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Diary.......     Top events........\par \f28 \par \par \uc2