\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Battered yen slumps further in U.S. trade. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Elizabeth Lazarowitz \par \uc2 873 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Januar 2000\par 17:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Jan 11 (Reuters) - The Japanese yen fell to seven-week lows against the dollar and Europe's single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in U.S. trading on Tuesday as dealers worried that global leaders may soon endorse Japanese efforts to weaken the yen. \par \par \uc2  Talk that Tokyo might try to enlist the help of G7 finance ministers and central bankers in taming the yen at their Jan. 22 meeting put the yen under broad-based pressure, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think anybody believes there will be coordinated or concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . I think there are fears there may be a more strongly worded statement," said Mike Malpede, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Refco Ltd. \par \par \uc2  As the New York session started, the euro swiftly jumped as high as 109.56 yen, its highest level since Nov. 22. Even though the euro soon fell half a yen to slip below 109 yen, it held onto a gains, trading up more than three-quarters of a percent. \par \par \uc2  The dollar also firmed against the yen to a fresh seven-week peak of 106.31 before retracing a part of its move to stand around 105.66 yen at 10:15 a.m. (1515 GMT), still up about half a percent from the prior close. \par \par \uc2  "People who have been short dollars for the past few months riding the whole way down got a little discouraged between the BoJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  down around 101.50 and the failure to get below 100," said Vincent Palazzolo, chief dealer at Sumitomo Bank New York. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets last week. This was the 14th time the bank had sold yen on the open market since June 1999, hoping to curb the yen's industry-crippling rise. \par \par \uc2  Despite the dollar's gains against the yen, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had less luck against European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as traders worried about the performance of U.S. equities. \par \par \uc2  Stocks began Tuesday's session mixed, with the Dow Jones industrial average up 10 points at 11,582, as the markets awaited a crush of earnings reports. \par \par \uc2  At 10:15 a.m. (1515 GMT), the euro stood near $1.0297, up about 0.38 percent from Monday's close near $1.0250. \par \par \uc2  The euro ticked slightly lower in late European trading after German engineering union IG Metall said on Tuesday its board recommended a pay raise of up to 5.5 percent for 2000. \par \par \uc2  Analysts called the pay demand excessive and said it might spark fresh fears of inflationary dangers, something \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders said helped dent the euro briefly. \par \par \uc2  "I think people will interpret that as putting potentially inflationary pressure inside the euro block," weighing on the euro, said Rick Gomes, managing director of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at HSBC in New York. \par \par \uc2  Dealers predicted the euro could push higher if U.S. asset market declines weigh on the dollar, but the European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to run into technical resistance near $1.0330 and 109.30 yen, close to its overnight highs. \par \par \uc2  Wall Street has been on a rally since late last week and jumped on the news Internet provider AOL and media giant Time Warner Inc. plan to merge, but some dealers said profit-taking or negative earnings news could unhinge the rally. \par \par \uc2  The yen came under pressure in Asian trading amid market talk that rating agency Standard & Poor's would make a negative announcement on Japan's credit standing. Although a speech from S&P President Leo O'Neill in Tokyo later reaffirmed Japan's top triple-A rating, dollar/yen held its ground and went on to extend its gains. \par \par \uc2  "There has been reasonably good interest to buy although the volumes have been quite low, but the rumour that S&P was going to downgrade Japan helped contribute to the yen selling," said Cameron Crise at Warburg Dillon Read. \par \par \uc2  ((U.S. Financial Markets Desk, 212-859-1607)). \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 10:25 a.m. (1525 GMT).  All data taken \par \par \uc2  from Reuters with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. \par \par \uc2  close at 4:30 p.m. (2130 GMT). \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab    Last     US Close  %Chg   YTD %     1999\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab Jan. 10\tab \tab \tab  Close\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/dlr\tab \tab    1.0298   1.0253   +0.44   +2.26   1.0070\par Dlr/yen\tab \tab     105.64   105.10   +0.51   +3.36   102.21\par Euro/yen\tab \tab    108.76   107.80   +0.89   +5.49   103.10\par Dlr/swiss\tab \tab   1.5616   1.5680   -0.41   -1.80   1.5902\par Stg/dlr\tab \tab     1.6462   1.6365   +0.59   +1.77   1.6176\par Can/dlr\tab \tab     1.4560   1.4550   +0.07   +0.73   1.4455\par Aus/dlr\tab \tab     0.6573   0.6560   +0.20   +0.15   0.6563\par Euro/swiss\tab \tab  1.6089   1.6093   -0.02   +0.33   1.6036\par Euro/stg\tab \tab    0.6253   0.6260   -0.11   +0.22   0.6239\par  All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news ...\tab     Debt...   Indicators...\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports..\tab \tab \tab \tab \par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \par \par All spots\tab \par Tokyo spots\tab \p