\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro rallies as yen takes a tumble. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Elizabeth Lazarowitz \par \uc2 802 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Januar 2000\par 23:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Jan 11 (Reuters) - The euro raced to seven-week \par \par \uc2  highs against the yen and rallied smartly against the dollar on \par \par \uc2  Tuesday, boosted by weakness on Wall Street and talk that \par \par \uc2  global leaders may help Japan weaken the yen. \par \par \uc2  The euro's gains against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also helped \par \par \uc2  the dollar extend recent gains against the yen to seven-week \par \par \uc2  peaks. \par \par \uc2  As U.S. trade closed, the euro was up over 1.5 percent \par \par \uc2  against the yen on the day at 109.58 yen, and rose more than \par \par \uc2  three quarters of a percent against the dollar to $1.0332. The \par \par \uc2  U.S. unit was up nearly 1 percent against the yen at 106.07. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the yen, which has lost ground steadily since \par \par \uc2  the start of the year, was weighed down afresh by speculation \par \par \uc2  Tokyo might persuade finance ministers and central bankers from \par \par \uc2  the Group of Seven wealthy nations meeting Jan. 22 to join \par \par \uc2  efforts to tame the yen. \par \par \uc2  "From the G7's point of view the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets are doing \par \par \uc2  what they want them to do," said \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Tim Fox at \par \par \uc2  Standard Chartered Bank. \par \par \uc2  "I doubt people believe there will be joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  but with the yen backing off a bit, the euro appreciating a \par \par \uc2  bit, there may be some language which gives explicit support of \par \par \uc2  recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trends." \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling yen on the \par \par \uc2  foreign exchanges at least 14 times since June 1999 to curb \par \par \uc2  industry-crippling strength in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Most recently it has been seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  several times in \par \par \uc2  a bid to prevent the yen rallying beyond the four-year highs \par \par \uc2  near 101.20 hit in December 1999. \par \par \uc2  A poor showing in U.S. asset markets had also helped lift \par \par \uc2  the euro against the dollar as jittery investors exited U.S. \par \par \uc2  assets. \par \par \uc2  At the close of trade the Dow Jones industrial average \par \par \uc2  stood 61 points, or half a percent lower, while the \par \par \uc2  technlogy-laden Nasdaq index shed 127 point or more than 3 \par \par \uc2  percent. \par \par \uc2  That reversed the course set on Monday when U.S. stocks - \par \par \uc2  and the dollar - rallied on news Internet provider America \par \par \uc2  Online Inc. and media giant Time Warner Inc. plan to merge. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the euro would continue to pin its hopes on \par \par \uc2  less buoyant U.S. asset markets, but that it would likely run \par \par \uc2  into technical resistance near the session highs. \par \par \uc2  The European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had little reaction to comments from \par \par \uc2  European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Vice President Christian Noyer, who said \par \par \uc2  U.S. and European growth rates should converge in 2000 and the \par \par \uc2  euro had room to rise. \par \par \uc2  "We're extremely confident that the potential of the \par \par \uc2  appreciation of the euro that does exist will develop in the \par \par \uc2  course of this year," said Noyer, speaking in Houston. \par \par \uc2  During European trading, the euro had ticked slightly lower \par \par \uc2  after German engineering union IG Metall said on Tuesday its \par \par \uc2  board recommended a pay raise of up to 5.5 percent for 2000. \par \par \uc2  Analysts called the pay demand excessive and said it might \par \par \uc2  spark fresh fears of inflationary dangers, something \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  traders said helped dent the euro briefly. \par \par \uc2  "I think people will interpret that as putting potentially \par \par \uc2  inflationary pressure inside the euro bloc," weighing on the \par \par \uc2  euro, said Rick Gomes, managing director of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at \par \par \uc2  HSBC in New York. \par \par \uc2  In other trade, sterling was sharply higher against the \par \par \uc2  dollar amid speculation that British interest rates could be \par \par \uc2  hiked as much as 50 basis points this week. \par \par \uc2  ((-U.S. Financial Markets Desk, 212-859-1607 )) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 2146GMT. All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. \par \par \uc2  close at 2130GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab    US Close US Close  %Chg   YTD %  1999\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Cls\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab    11 Jan.  10 Jan.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/dlr\tab \tab    1.0332   1.0253   +0.77   +1.82   1.0070\par Dlr/yen\tab \tab     106.07   105.10   +0.92   +2.83   102.21\par Euro/yen\tab \tab    109.58   107.80   +1.65   +4.56   103.10\par Dlr/swiss\tab \tab   1.5580   1.5680   -0.64   -1.40   1.5902\par Stg/dlr\tab \tab     1.6480   1.6365   +0.70   +1.17   1.6176\par Dlr/can\tab \tab     1.4573   1.4550