\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar up versus euro on U.S. stocks optimism. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Elizabeth Lazarowitz \par \uc2 784 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Januar 2000\par 16:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Jan 10 (Reuters) - The dollar was firmer against Europe's single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in New York trading on Monday as dealers hope Wall Street's recovery will receive a shot in the arm from the world's largest takeover ever. \par \par \uc2  Top Internet services provider America Online Inc.  said it will buy Time Warner Inc. , the world's largest media company, for about $190 billion in stock. The Dow Jones industrial average applauded the move, rising over 100 points in the first half hour of trading. \par \par \uc2  The dollar had already begun to chip away at the euro's sizable gains last week and the trend continued overnight. \par \par \uc2  As New York trading got underway, the European single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was about half a percent lower from its prior close against the greenback near $1.0240, after flirting with one-week lows just above $1.02 overnight. \par \par \uc2  "The U.S. stock market is the key," said David Gilmore, partner at \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Analytics in Essex, Connecticut. "We're unwinding the damage from last week." \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar was also 0.4-percent firmer from Friday's close against the Swiss franc\tab   just above 1.57 francs after rallying to a one-week high of 1.5748 francs.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Meanwhile, the greenback was modestly softer against the Japanese yen as it struggled to recover from a bout of profit-taking overnight that drove it as low as 104.37 yen, almost 1.5 percent below Friday's high near 106 yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro's weakness against the yen had also helped the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gain a toehold against the dollar, dealers said. The euro sagged near 107.80 yen in early U.S. trading, about half a percent from Friday's close.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "That \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pair picked up some ground last week, and there's probably some consolidation going on," said John Hazelton, trader at PNC Bank in Pittsburgh.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Traders said the yen recovery was mainly a technical correction, with price movements exaggerated by thin volume due to a holiday in Japan.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Senior finance ministers at a closely-watched Group of Seven (G7) meeting this weekend in Tokyo were mum on the record about the yen, relieving dealers' concerns about the possibility of joint \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Kyodo news agency reported \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had urged other nations to cooperate in efforts to bring down the yen's value. However, traders said no joint \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was expected.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said lingering concern that the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets to dampen the yen's recent strength would limit the dollar's decline. The BoJ bought dollars for yen early last week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts said the primary short-term trend remained in favour of the dollar and the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could break above 105.00 yen on Monday if U.S. assets posted another day of strong gains.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The relationship between the dollar and U.S. stocks is going to continue for the next couple of weeks," said Jesper Dannesboe, treasury economist at ABN AMRO in London.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Meanwhile, the market paid little attention to comments made by European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  officials over the weekend.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ECB board member Sirkka Hamalainen said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  saw no reason for a rate change at the moment but would remain vigilant on prices and secondary factors.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ECB chief economist Otmar Issing said European inflation was likely to peak in the months ahead and a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  emphasis on price stability gave the euro "strong potential" to rise.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par French Finance Minister Christian Sautter also said he believed last November's hike in euro zone interest rates was sufficient and the euro had potential to rise.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((U.S. Financial Markets Desk, 212 859-1607))\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 10:06 a.m. (1506 GMT).  All data taken from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Reuters with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par at 4:30 p.m. (2130 GMT).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Last     US Close  %Chg   YTD %    1999\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Jan. 07\tab \tab \tab  Close\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/dlr\tab \tab    1.0245   1.0289   -0.43   +1.74   1.0070\par Dlr/yen\tab \tab     105.21   105.35   -0.13   +2.94   102.21\par Euro/yen\tab \tab    107.77   108.36   -0.54   +4.53   103.10\par Dlr/swiss\tab \tab   1.5692   1.5645   +0.30   -1.32   1.5902\par Stg/dlr\tab \tab     1.6376   1.6383   -0.04   +1.24   1.6176\par Can/dlr\tab \tab     1.4536   1.4553   -0.12   +0.56   1.4455\par Aus/dlr\tab \tab     0.6556   0.6548   +0.12   -0.11   0.6563\par Euro/swiss\tab \tab  1.6083   1.6092   -0.06   +0.29   1.6036\par Euro/stg\tab \tab    0.6251   0.6280   -0.46   +0.19   0.6239\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw1a03mtc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
