\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar consolidates after big reversal week. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Shinichi Kishima \par \uc2 895 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Januar 2000\par 12:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par LONDON, Jan 7 (Reuters) - The dollar pulled back after a brief probe of six-week highs against the yen\tab   on Friday and consolidated above Thursday's seven-week lows against the euro amid pre-weekend position squaring.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par As the first week of 2000 - which has seen a dramatic reversal from last year's trend - drew to a close, caution reigned ahead of the closely watched U.S. employment report due out at 1330 GMT and a Group of Seven deputy finance ministers' meeting at the weekend, traders said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  "When you get these sort of sharp moves in relatively thin conditions, obviously you do need some consolidation and the foundations have stabilised a bit. At the moment that's what the market is doing in both dollar/yen and euro/dollar," said Mark Henry, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at GNI in London. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar had risen 4.2 percent this week to a 105.58 yen peak set earlier in the session before pulling back to around 105 yen. The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Tuesday has kept the market wary of selling the dollar throughout the week, while gains in euro/dollar\tab   triggered a broad retreat in the yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro was about a cent off Thursday's $1.0414 seven-week high against the dollar - a gain of 3.6 percent on the week - as the broader U.S. stock market showed a sign of stabilising after a fierce sell-off at the start of the week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Although the Nasdaq composite\tab   , heavily laden with volatile high-tech stocks, extended losses with a 3.88-percent drop on Thursday, the Dow Jones industrial average bounced 1.17 percent, a move many analysts saw as a reasonable correction after last year's frenzy over high-tech stocks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "It does seem to be a switching out of tech stocks into blue chips, and that sort of shift is supportive of the dollar than a more wide-spread equity market weakness," said Michael Lewis, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  economist at Deutsche Bank in London.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts said the outlook for a sustained recovery in both dollar/yen and euro/dollar had greatly improved this week, but that a lot still hinged on how the U.S. asset market fared, which in turn would be driven by expectations about the U.S. Federal Reserve's monetary policy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. EMPLOYMENT DATA IN FOCUS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par To that end, the December jobs data, particularly average earnings figures, could be a key pointer for the market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "If you think interest rates have been the key factor in what's been going on in the U.S. (stock market)...then certainly that's been the factor that's contributed to the euro's performance since the start of the year," GNI's Henry said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Economists polled by Reuters have forecast, on average, a rise of 0.3 percent in average hourly earnings and a 224,000 increase in non-farm payrolls in December.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Another key factor for dollar/yen would be the weekend G7D meeting, which lays the ground for the main finance ministers' meeting later this month.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The risk for dollar/yen to break below 100 is currently gone due to the hopes of the G7 meetings," said Michael Rottmann, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at HypoVereinsbank in Munich.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He said while no substantial message for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets was likely after this weekend's meeting, the market was looking for a strong statement after the main G7 meeting.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We will probably get another statement within the communique that the G7 partners are still in favour of a somewhat weaker yen, or at least of a stable yen."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Japan's commitment to stemming the yen's appreciation was reconfirmed when Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa said during Asian trading that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would need to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market if any rapid movements were detected.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He added that he had told the ministry late last year to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market if the dollar looked set to fall below 100 yen. ((London Capital Markets +44-171-542-6721, shinichi.kishima@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 1109 GMT. All data taken from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Reuters, with percent change calculated from the daily U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par close at 2130 GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab \tab Last   US Close  % Chg   YTD %    1999\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   06 Jan\tab \tab \tab   close\par \tab \tab \tab     -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr\tab \tab     1.0300   1.0319   -0.18   +2.28   1.0070\par  Dlr/yen\tab \tab      105.03   105.31   -0.27   +2.76   102.21\par  Euro/yen\tab \tab     108.17   108.71   -0.50   +4.91   103.10\par  Dlr/sw