\par\par \b \uc2  G7 Deps Weekend Meeting In Tokyo Eyed For  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Stance \b0\par\par\uc2 565 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Januar 2000\par 13:34\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  FRANKFURT -(Dow Jones)- High-level representatives of the worlds' richest nations are meeting this weekend in Tokyo, and financial markets are particularly anxious to learn whether the Group of Seven is gearing up to support Japan's efforts to weaken the yen. \par \par \uc2  Recent statements from western officials show no special concern about the yen's appreciation. But Japan's fear a stronger yen will stifle the country's budding economy is very much alive, with the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  having \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  just this week for the second time in less than a month. \par \par \uc2  The meeting largely serves to lay the groundwork for a meeting of G7 finance ministers and central bankers in Tokyo on Jan. 22. \par \par \uc2  Half of the weekend's meeting will be dedicated to routine matters, such as market surveillance, an Italian Treasury source said. The other half will include an ongoing discussion of the private sector's involvement in financial crises. Russia, and the recent change of leadership there, will also play a role in the talks. \par \par \uc2  Topics won't likely include any detailed discussion of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels or regimes, a U.K. Treasury spokesman said. \par \par \uc2  Haruhiko Kuroda, Japan's vice finance minister for international affairs, and German deputy finance minister Caio Koch-Weser met Friday in Tokyo ahead of the meeting. \par \par \uc2  Kuroda said the two didn't discuss \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at their four-hour meeting. The statement prompted a steep fall in the dollar against the yen because markets didn't see a strong yen as a G7 priority. \par \par \uc2  In September, G7 ministers released a statement supporting Japan's worries about a recently strengthening yen. While Tokyo officials have touted that statement repeatedly since then, there has been no sign of any coordinated action among G7 countries to curb the yen's rise against the dollar and the euro. \par \par \uc2  Koch-Weser, after the meeting with his Japanese counterpart, said that at their gathering on Jan. 22 the G7, by tradition, would discuss the standard issues of economic surveillance and exchange rates. He wouldn't comment on the euro's level Friday. \par \par \uc2  "It would be inappropriate to comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  issues ahead of the (G7) deputy finance ministers' meeting this weekend and the ministers' meeting later this month in Tokyo," he said. \par \par \uc2  G7 deputies usually keep a lid on their public statements. They prefer to defer to their bosses, the ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  heads. \par \par \uc2  As late as last Wednesday, the ECB made clear it hadn't yet been contacted by Japan regarding exchange rates. The ECB takes part in G7 discussions, and ECB executive board member Tommaso Padoa-Schioppa will represent the ECB at the weekend meeting. \par \par \uc2  "The Japanese have not yet been in touch with me, nor with others, about what they want to discuss in Tokyo on exchange rates," ECB President Wim Duisenberg said at a press conference on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "I think that the attitude of the monetary authorities of Europe and the United States will remain - that we will closely watch the exchange rate developments between the three major economic areas, but that, for us, these developments do not give rise to a change in our attitude or policies," he said. \par \par \uc2  -By G. Thomas Sims; 4969 29725 500; tom.sims@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  With contributions from Ralph Traviato in Rome and Chip Cummins in London. \par \par \uc2  1195 4212 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw170059a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
