\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -2: Japan's Yen-Weakening Efforts Paying Off \b0\par\par\uc2 392 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Januar 2000\par 07:06\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Many market watchers note that as the dollar's trading range is shifting upward against the yen even as it weakens against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been quite effective. \par \par \uc2  The effects of the actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  have also been invigorated by verbal backing from Finance Ministry officials. \par \par \uc2  For instance, in a rare interview published Wednesday in Japan's leading financial newspaper, Haruhiko Kuroda, the vice finance minister for international affairs, stressed that the ministry's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy isn't limited to smoothing out disruptive moves in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Kuroda said of Tuesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 : "By acting in the market, we corrected an overshooting in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates. But it's not the case that we only aim to calm rough moves in the market. Depending on conditions, we will cooperate with (other Group of Seven nations) or act on our own to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . And when we act, we will act boldly." \par \par \uc2  Kuroda, as well as the ministry's international bureau head Zembei Mizoguchi, also said that the yen was still "too strong" when the dollar was buying around Y104.20. Mizoguchi also told reporters Thursday that "a further correction to the excessively strong yen is desirable." \par \par \uc2  "The fact that the dollar has risen only against the yen and fallen against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  shows that the market is taking \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears rather seriously," said a dealer at a Japanese trust bank. \par \par \uc2  After the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  made its presence clear on the first trading day of the year, and in light of all the official jawboning, "it's become more difficult to sell the dollar," said a trader at a European bank in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  However, most dealers said that current moves aren't enough to declare that the dollar is on a concrete upward track against the yen, and that much of its gains stems from the euro's strength versus the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y107.87, up from Y107.59 in New York late Wednesday. The euro was at Y106.18 in Tokyo late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.6443, up from $1.6425 in New York late Wednesday. Sterling was at $1.6375 in Tokyo late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  -By Chang-Ran Kim; 813-5255-2929; chang-ran.kim@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw16002bs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
