\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro milks Dow drop, hits 7-week high vs dlr. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 535 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2000\par 11:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Jan 5 (Reuters) - The euro rose to seven-week highs against the dollar on Wednesday, as concerns over U.S. assets contrasted with increased optimism over European economic growth. \par \par \uc2  The euro climbed to $1.0402, its highest since November 18 and a gain of 3-1/2 cents from this year's lows set on Monday, on fears that the Dow Jones Industrial Average, which tumbled more than three percent on Tuesday, could be in for a major correction after a decade-long bull run. \par \par \uc2  "There seems to be a lot of momentum behind this move, but it is really the weakness of U.S. stocks that has been driving it," said Johnathan Bayley, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Paribas in Paris. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said falling U.S. stocks and bonds reflected worries the U.S. Federal Reserve could raise interest rates when it meets in February. \par \par \uc2  But automated March S&P futures were up 8.00 points by 1044 GMT, indicating a stronger open to the Dow, while the euro eased to around $1.0365. The euro found support early in European trade from German unemployment data, leaked on Tuesday and released officially on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The German jobless total fell by a seasonally adjusted 68,000 in December from the previous month, though the unemployment rate ticked up to 10.3 percent from 10.0 percent in November. German Federal Labour Office President Bernhard Jagoda said he expected the jobless total to fall further in January. \par \par \uc2  German and Eurozone sector surveys showed the sector contined to expand in December, but at a slower pace than previously. \par \par \uc2  The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  holds its first meeting of 2000 on Wednesday, but no change in interest rates is expected. \par \par \uc2  YEN WARINESS OF BOJ \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen, meanwhile, rose to 2-1/2 week highs of 103.47, boosted by gains in the euro to six-week highs against the yen, traders said. The impact of the Dow sell-off was also somewhat offset by a 2.42-percent drop in the Tokyo stock market's Nikkei average, they added. \par \par \uc2  Wariness to sell dollars too aggresively also persisted after Tuesday's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which had pushed the dollar up to the 103-area after a test of four-year lows near 101 set last month. \par \par \uc2  Although bullishness on the Nikkei has been cited as a major reason for the yen's ascent since mid-1999, the impact of Wednesday's selloff was diluted by an apparent lack of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly related to it, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar could be supported if foreign investors sell Tokyo stocks and buy dollars to repatriate their funds, but it is unclear yet whether such \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  are taking place," said a dealer at a Japanese bank in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  If anything, dealers said the Nikkei's pullback could be seen as a bargain-hunting opportunity by overseas investors. \par \par \uc2  But senior Japanese Finance Ministry official Zembei Mizoguchi earlier on Wednesday reiterated the yen's rise since last summer was undesirable and the ministry would take appropriate action as needed in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw15083rm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
