\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro clocks up gains for 3rd day, eyes Dow. \b0\par\par\uc2 856 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2000\par 16:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Jan 5 (Reuters) - The euro, in a third straight day of gains, traded at seven-week highs against the dollar and six-week highs versus the yen on Wednesday amid optimism about Europe's economy and worries on Wall Street. \par \par \uc2  Jockeying for postions by investors, who were relieved by a smooth millennium switchover, also played a key role in the euro's rise, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The euro was unfazed after European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left interest rates unchanged, as expected, and was similarly relaxed about comments from ECB officials following their meeting. \par \par \uc2  "(ECB President Wim) Duisenberg has spewed forth the ECB's mantra, right in line with expectations - there's no reason to buy or sell on it," said David Gilmore, partner at \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Analytics. \par \par \uc2  Duisenberg said he was pleased to see the euro had moved up and away from the psychologically important one-to-one level with the dollar briefly hit late last year. \par \par \uc2  He also repeated his forecast that he expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would rise, and commenting on the euro's rise in recent days, Duisenberg told a news conference "so far, so good." \par \par \uc2  The dollar, meanwhile, notched up fresh gains against the Japanese yen, building on a rally started Tuesday when the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to tame the strong yen. Traders linked the day's move up to the yen's declines against the euro. \par \par \uc2  The dollar rallied, climbing to a five-week high against the yen above 103.78 in U.S. trade, which was up more than two full yen from the week's low. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro, meanwhile, was up half a percent against the dollar at $1.0356\tab  , after peaking overnight at $1.0402, its highest since Nov. 18, 1999, and a gain of 3-1/2 cents from this year's lows set on Monday.\par The euro was also up over three-quarters of a percent against the yen \tab   at 107.26 yen. Its overnight high of 107.70 was up more than five yen from the year's low and the highest level since Nov. 23, 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was underpinned overnight by data showing that the German jobless total fell by a seasonally adjusted 68,000 in December from the previous month, though the unemployment rate ticked up to 10.3 percent from 10.0 percent in November.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par German and Eurozone service sector surveys showed that these sectors continued to expand in December, but at a slower pace than previously.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Traders said the market was keeping a close eye on the U.S. stock market, whose steep declines this week amid interest rate fears weighed on the dollar. The Dow Jones industrial average was 35 points shortly after opening, but the technology-heavy Nasdaq fell 53 points.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But many traders said repositioning by big market players was a key factor in the large, often volatile market moves this week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "There seems to be some New Year profit-taking on euro/yen, said Dennis Heidt, chief dealer at Banque Paribas. "Maybe some hedge funds are unwinding their positions from the previous year, comfortable that any Y2K problems are behind them."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par This suggested that the euro's stellar rise and the dollar's rebound about the yen may lack staying power once the profit-taking and positioning is done, Gilmore said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "It hasn't been fundamentals over the past two days. It's all about market position," Gilmore said. "People have been very short euro versus the yen and the dollar and short the dollar versus the yen. And what we're seeing now is people balancing positions, booking profits."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Wariness to sell dollars too aggressively also persisted after Tuesday's Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which had pushed the dollar up to the 103-area after a test of four-year lows near 101 set last month.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 1433GMT.  All data taken from Reuters\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with percent change calculated from the daily U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par close at 2130GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab    Last     US Close  %Chg   YTD %  1999\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Cls\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab 04 Jan.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/dlr\tab \tab    1.0356   1.0308   +0.47   +2.84   1.0070\par Dlr/yen\tab \tab     103.61   103.25   +0.35   +1.37   102.21\par Euro/yen\tab \tab    107.26   106.40   +0.81   +4.03   103.10\par Dlr/swiss\tab \tab   1.5496   1.5552   -0.36   -2.55   1.5902\par Stg/dlr\tab \tab     1.6386   1.6365   +0.13   +1.30   1.6176\par Can/dlr\tab \tab     1.4520   1.4518   +0.01   +0.45   1.4455\par Aus/dlr\tab \tab     0.6586   0.6548   +0.58   +0.35   0.6563\par Euro/swiss\tab \tab  1.6047   1.6037   +0.06   +0.07   1.6036\par Euro/stg\tab \tab    0.6317   0.6296   +0.33   +1.25   0.6239\par     ..\tab     Debt...   Indicators...\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports..\tab \tab \tab \tab \par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \par \par All spots\tab \par Tokyo spots\tab \par Europe spots\tab \par Volatilities\tab \par Tokyo \f28 \