\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro holds gains as Wall Street buckles. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Svea Herbst-Bayliss \par \uc2 750 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Januar 2000\par 23:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Jan 4 (Reuters) - The euro extended its birthday rally on Tuesday, the second trading day of 2000 when dealers welcomed signs of stronger growth in Europe and worried about Wall Street's health as U.S. stocks tumbled for a second day. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, positive European manufacturing data and tumbling U.S. asset markets sparked the euro's rally which continued overnight. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At the close of New York trading, the one-year old euro commanded a nearly 2-1/4 percent gain on the yen\tab      to stand at 106.40 yen. It also gained more than half a percent on the British pound to 62.96 pence and rose 0.45 percent against the dollar to $1.0308.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the two trading days of 2000, the adolescent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has gained nearly two percent in value against the dollar and almost one percent against the yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We think the lows have been seen for the euro," said Robert Sinche, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at Citibank in New York. "You have both improving cyclical conditions in the euro area and the risk in U.S. asset prices pushing the euro higher."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The selling spree on Wall Street continued on Tuesday against a background of rising U.S. bond yields and fears the Federal Reserve will raise interest rates more aggressively than previously expected to help cool the red-hot economy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Dow Jones industrial average tumbled 3.17 percent, falling nearly 360 points to 10997.93 while the technology laden NASDAQ was even harder hit and posted a 5.56 percent loss at 3901.49 one day after setting a record high.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Overnight the euro received a small boost when Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  again sold its own \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on the open market in order to prevent a rapidly strengthening yen from choking off the nation's fragile economic recovery.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par For the third time since November, the Bank of Japan acted to block the yen's rise to 101.00 to the dollar when the yen hit a four-year high of 101.25. At the close, the dollar\tab   stood at 103.25 yen, up over 1-1/2 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "This looks like a gentle reminder from the Japanese authorities that they're really uncomfortable with the level of the exchange rate Citibank's Sinche said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Fears there may be more \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the days before a meeting in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of the Group of Seven rich nations kept the yen wedged in a relatively tight trading range.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par While traders and analysts cheered the euro's new gains, many questioned the rally's durability, noting there may be big obstacles to more gains above the $1.0450 level.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The jury is still out on growth in Europe and that is why the euro came off a little from its session highs," at $1.0343 explained Banc One Capital Markets vice president Ralph DelZenero in Chicago.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We've come two-and-a half, almost three cents in the last day-and-a-half, so we've seen a pretty significant move, and I think that we've just run out of steam a little bit," added Bob Houck, trader at Norwest Bank in Minneapolis.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets shrugged off news that President Bill Clinton nominated Alan Greenspan to a fourth term as chairman of the Federal Reserve Board, a move which dealers said had been widely expected and should be positive for the dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 2214GMT. All data taken from Reuters with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab US Close US Close  %Chg   YTD %  1999 Cls\par \tab \tab \tab 04 Jan.  03 Jan.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  -------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/dlr\tab \tab    1.0308   1.0262   +0.45   +1.91   1.0070\par  Dlr/yen\tab \tab     103.25   101.56   +1.66   -0.64   102.21\par  Euro/yen\tab \tab    106.40   104.09   +2.22   +0.96   103.10\par  Dlr/swiss\tab \tab   1.5552   1.5645   -0.59   -1.62   1.5902\par  Stg/dlr\tab \tab     1.6365   1.6368   -0.02   +1.19   1.6176\par  Dlr/can\tab \tab     1.4518   1.4461   +0.39   +0.04   1.4455\par  Aus/dlr\tab \tab     0.6548   0.6579   -0.47   +0.24   0.6563\par  Euro/swiss\tab \tab  1.6037   1.6045   -0.05   +0.06   1.6036\par  Euro/stg\tab \tab    0.6296   0.6261   +0.56   +0.35   0.6239\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((-Svea Herbst-Bayliss, U.S. Financial Markets Desk, 212-859-1639 )).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dw1401krt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
