\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro/dollar firms to six-week highs. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Deepthi Wickremasinghe \par \uc2 622 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Januar 2000\par 14:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Jan 4 (Reuters) - The euro extended its gains against the dollar on Tuesday speeding up to six-week highs but analysts were sceptical about how long gains could be sustained. \par \par \uc2  The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has risen almost three percent against the dollar since trading resumed following the New Year holidays, hitting its highest since November 23. Yet despite expectations of a pick up in European growth, analysts said there was little new in the fundamental outlook which had triggered the euro's recent demise. \par \par \uc2  "A rally in the euro is not sustainable on fundamental grounds," said Steve Barrow, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bear Stearns in London. \par \par \uc2  "Euroland is entering a situation where inflation dangers are creeping up and until the market is convinced that the ECB (European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) can do the job and keep inflation below two percent it won't give the ECB or the euro the benefit of the doubt." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Tuesday's rise in euro/dollar had been triggered by stop-loss orders to buy the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  around $1.0280, which was the 31.8 percent Fibonacci retracement of the fall from mid-October highs above $1.09 to all time lows just below parity in early December. \par \par \uc2  "Liquidity is still pretty poor... but it is a market that is moving as more people get sucked in, so inevitably momentum can build up and we can get a reasonably sharp move, which is what we have seen today," said Barrow at Bear Stearns. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said while the setback for Dow Jones Industrials Average which closed 1.21 percent lower on Monday might undermine the dollar in the near term and thus help the euro to firm, it was unlikely to be sustained. \par \par \uc2  Tony Norfield head of global treasury research at ABN AMRO in London said the dollar had trended higher against the euro last year despite a number of major pullbacks in Wall Street stocks. \par \par \uc2  "This (Dow selloff) shouldn't have a long lasting effect because we've seen these things a number of times before," he said. We don't see this changing the trend." \par \par \uc2  For now however the euro's stronger position coupled with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars for yen had also helped push the euro to a six-week high against the yen. \par \par \uc2  "As long as the BOJ can prop up dollar/yen then euro/yen will continue to get a bit of a prop from that," said Bear Stearns' Barrow. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen rose around 1.7 percent on to a two-week high of 103.17 in European trade building on gains seen in Asia after the BOJ stepped into the market as the Japanese unit came within view of its 101.22 four-year peaks against the dollar set in November. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the underlying market perception that Japan may find support for its action in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market from its Group of Seven partners now that the millennium and Christmas holidays are over would likely curb further yen gains for now. \par \par \uc2  "Just the prospect of that is probably enough to stabilise things for the short term," said Joanne Collins, senior economist at Daiwa Europe in London. \par \par \uc2  Without support from the other members of G7 she said Japan was not likely to hit dollar/yen too hard but would be content to see it rising away from 101 yen. \par \par \uc2  "But if they can convince their G7 partners to be part of it...and if we saw a bit of a trend being established towards a weaker yen then we might see heavy handed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to really push it lower," said Collins. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dw1401k2b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
