\par\par \b \uc2  Kuroda declines comment on afternoon  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 197 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Januar 2000\par 07:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Jan 4 (Reuters) - Senior Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) official Haruhiko Kuroda said he could not comment on whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Tuesday afternoon. \par \par \uc2  Late in the morning, Kuroda, Japan's vice finance minister for international affairs, confirmed that Japan had acted in the market. The dollar jumped above 102 yen in late morning trade after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which acts as MOF's agent in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, was detected buying dollars for yen. \par \par \uc2  Bankers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was detected in the market again in the afternoon as the dollar slipped back toward 102 yen. \par \par \uc2  Asked whether Japanese monetary authorities took action again in the afternoon to prevent the yen's rise, Kuroda told Reuters, "We won't say when we acted. All we can say is that we took action today." \par \par \uc2  The dollar had slipped as low as 101.46 yen before the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushed it to a peak of 102.78. At 0645 GMT the dollar was quoted around 102.30/40 yen. ((Tokyo Newsroom, +813-3432-1396 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dw1401jqg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
