\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro buoyed vs dollar by pain on Wall Street. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Lida Poletz \par \uc2 783 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Januar 2000\par 16:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Jan 4 (Reuters) - The euro stood at six week highs against the dollar on Tuesday, heralding a strong start to the year, and dealers said more near term gains could follow if Wall Street's pain deepens. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, steep losses in U.S. stocks and bonds along with positive euro zone manufacturing data had triggered a blistering euro rally that continued overnight. \par \par \uc2  "We do think the lows have been seen for the euro," said Robert Sinche, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Citibank. "You have both improving cyclical conditions in the euro area and the risk in U.S. asset prices pushing the euro higher." \par \par \uc2  Investors in U.S. equities continued their selling spree in early trade on Tuesday against a background of high bond yields and fears the Federal Reserve will raise interest rates more aggressively than previously thought. \par \par \uc2  The Dow Jones industrial average fell one percent shortly after opening, while the technology-heavy Nasdaq tumbled 2 percent. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, at 9:30 a.m. (1430 GMT) the euro traded at $1.0316, up half a percent against the dollar compared to its previous New York close. At its overnight high of $1.0343, the euro was up nearly 3 percent from Monday's low. \par \par \uc2  Despite the euro's buoyancy, however, some traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would struggle to its extend gains as the market mulled Europe's fundamental outlook. \par \par \uc2  "Is it sustainable? We need to get a read in late-January or early February on if this story of Europe outgrowing the U.S. really can happen. Our assumptions are that it is not and the market is gettin bulled up over nothing," said Greg Anderson, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Fleet Boston. \par \par \uc2  Concerns about Europe's growth prospects and a red-hot U.S. economic performance and promped the euro to lose 15 percent of its value against the dollar last year. \par \par \uc2  "The market is still feeling extremely cautious about the euro here," said John Schein, vice president at Fortis. "I still don't trust it." \par \par \uc2  Despite the dollar's declines against the euro, it remained sharply higher against the yen following overnight \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The BoJ acted for the third time block the yen's rise to 101.00 to the dollar since last November when the yen hit a four-year high of 101.25. \par \par \uc2  In early U.S. trade the dollar was off a touch from overnight highs but was still up nearly 1.5 percent at 103.01 yen. Caution about further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would help support the dollar during U.S. trade, although there was little concern that the BOJ might act during U.S. trading hours. \par \par \uc2  "This looks like a gentle reminder from the Japanese authorities that they're really uncomfortable with the level of the exchange rate," said Sinche. "But clearly this is not a coordinated effort with the U.S. and Europe - I would not even expect to see the BOJ during the U.S. session. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile enthusiasm for Japanese stocks continues, with Tokyo's benchmark Nikkei 225 share index leaping 250 points at one stage to its highest level since August. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro's stronger position coupled with BOJ \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had also helped push the euro to a six-week high against the yen\tab     .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At 106.30 yen, the euro was up more than 2 percent from theprevious day's close.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 1429GMT. All data taken from Reuters with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab      Last     US Close  %Chg   YTD %  1999 Cls\par \tab \tab \tab \tab    03 Jan.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  -------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/dlr\tab \tab    1.0316   1.0262   +0.53   +2.44   1.0070\par  Dlr/yen\tab \tab     103.01   101.56   +1.43   +0.78   102.21\par  Euro/yen\tab \tab    106.30   104.09   +2.12   +3.10   103.10\par  Dlr/swiss\tab \tab   1.5552   1.5645   -0.59   -2.20   1.5902\par  Stg/dlr\tab \tab     1.6358   1.6368   -0.06   +1.13   1.6176\par  Can/dlr\tab \tab     1.4491   1.4461   +0.21   +0.25   1.4455\par  Aus/dlr\tab \tab     0.6575   0.6579   -0.06   +0.18   0.6563\par  Euro/swiss\tab \tab  1.6051   1.6045   +0.04   +0.09   1.6036\par  Euro/stg\tab \tab    0.6306   0.6261   +0.72   +1.07   0.6239\par  ..\tab     Debt...   Indicators...\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports..\tab \tab \tab \tab \par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \par All spots\tab  Tokyo spots\tab   Europe spots\tab   Volatilities \tab Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market info from BOJ\tab    World \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Economic Forecasts...     Official rates...\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Diary.......     Top events........\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Diaries...........   Diaries Index........\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Press Digests....    Polls on G7 economies..\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Reuters Television.   European markets......\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((U.S. Finan