\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar/yen bounces, but gains seen fragile. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Shinichi Kishima \par \uc2 735 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Januar 2000\par 09:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Jan 4 (Reuters) - The dollar rose to one-week highs against the yen on Tuesday after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt an export-crippling yen rise, although most traders did not see any major trend reversal in the offing. \par \par \uc2  The dollar jumped some 1.5 percent to around 103 yen after the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but traders said the bounce was hardly convincing after an 18-percent loss from mid-1999 highs and in the face of growing bullishness on Japanese equities. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was generally weak, hovering near four-week lows against the euro set on Monday, undermined by a setback in the Dow Jones Industrial Average on concern of a U.S. Federal Reserve interest rate increase early this year. \par \par \uc2  "There's been hardly any bounce in dollar/yen," said Tony Norfield, head of global treasury research at ABN AMRO in London. "We think they (Japanese authorities) are effectively going to fight a losing battle. We see dollar/yen going down to 100 in the coming weeks." \par \par \uc2  The dollar initially sagged against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to 101.46 yen, not too far from a four-year low of 101.22 yen set in November, before the BOJ began buying the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The BOJ stepped in today as it had to absorb (dollar) selling orders for now," said a European bank dealer in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese Finance Ministry was quick to confirm the BOJ action, and its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Haruhiko Kuroda warned that authorities stood ready to act as necessary. \par \par \uc2  "We looked at the market's condition this morning and acted," Kuroda told reporters. "We will continue to watch the market carefully and will act decisively as necessary." \par \par \uc2  Yet traders said the greenback's recovery was modest at best considering the billions of dollars the BOJ probably bought. \par \par \uc2  Many overseas investors were still underweight in the buoyant Japanese equities and Japanese investors were scaling back their overseas investments, putting an upward pressure on the yen, they noted. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo's benchmark Nikkei 225 share index jumped 250 points at one stage on Tuesday morning to as high as 19,187, its highest level since August 1997. \par \par \uc2  Against the euro, the dollar held in a relatively tight range just below Monday's $1.0280 four-week low. \par \par \uc2  The euro was seen benefiting from a softer U.S. purchasing managers index for December, contrasting with robust PMIs out of Europe that came out on Monday, coupled unwinding of year-end safe-haven dollar buying. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at a U.S. bank in London said, however, that the euro's strength might not last very long. \par \par \uc2  "You may see that (euro buying) as a trend this week - people going back into the euro - but I don't think it's going to be a huge directional move." \par \par \uc2  Norfield at ABN AMRO agreed, adding the dollar had trended higher against the euro last year despite a number of major pullbacks in Wall Street stocks. \par \par \uc2  "This (Dow selloff) shouldn't have a long lasting effect because we've seen these things a number of times before," he said. We don't see this changing the trend." \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0843 GMT. All data taken from \par \par \uc2  Reuters, with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. \par \par \uc2  close at 2130 GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab \tab Last   US Close  % Chg   YTD % 