\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar Climbs Sharply Against Yen After Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Japan Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 1,154 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Januar 2000\par 06:37\par \uc2  Dow Jones Business News \par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK -(Dow Jones)- The dollar rose sharply against the yen Tuesday after the Bank of Japan made yet another attempt to rein in the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as Tokyo's financial markets reopened for the new year. Meanwhile, the euro posted a modest rise against the dollar, hitting a six-week high against its U.S. counterpart as stocks tumbled. \par \par \uc2  Late Tuesday in New York, the dollar was quoted at 103.27 yen, up from 101.65 yen late Monday in New York. The euro was quoted at $1.0304, up from $1.0258 late Monday in New York. The euro jumped as high as $1.0343 - more than a 38% retracement from the sell off of mid-October. The British pound was at $1.6365, little changed from $1.6370 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  In addition to the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a rebound in Treasurys prices amid a plunge in stocks on mounting concerns about higher interest rates helped support the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Nasdaq Composite index plunged more than 229 points, or 5.6% - its worst single-day point loss ever. The Nasdaq had soared nearly 86% in 1999. \par \par \uc2  The Dow Jones Industrial Average tumbled 359.58 points, or 3.2%, to 10997.93, on speculation that the Federal Reserve may be considering a increase in interest rates when it meets in early February. It was the blue-chip Dow's fourth largest loss ever. \par \par \uc2  In Asian dealings overnight, the Bank of Japan sold yen for dollars overnight in Asia when the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading around 101.50 yen and again near 102 yen, said dealers. After the Tokyo stock market closed, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again, lifting the dollar to 103.15 yen. \par \par \uc2  What was remarkable about the dollar's reaction to the BOJ's latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  wasn't its nearly one-and-a-half yen jump, but that it largely stayed up there, traders observed. For perhaps the first time in a year, BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  during Asian trading has had a dollar-boosting effect that extended into the New York trading session. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ's earlier efforts at \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been less than effective, and other traders believe the latest attempt will also be doomed to failure unless \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  can persuade the U.S. and European governments to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  as well, something they have shown little inclination to do. \par \par \uc2  "You can't say the Bank of Japan has finally got the yen under control based on 12 hours or so of yen-weakness," noted Ann Parker Mills, senior economist for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Brown Brothers Harriman in New York. \par \par \uc2  In fact, it would appear that the BOJ's success Tuesday may have simply come by default. Thin, post-Y2K conditions and a market that's distracted by other matters, including some recovery in the euro and a shaky start to the new year in U.S. asset markets, have worked in the BOJ's favor, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think anyone is suddenly any more alarmed about BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said David Gilmore, a partner at \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Analytics in Essex, Conn. "It is just a matter of timing." \par \par \uc2  Japanese officials have been worried about the yen's appreciation because it makes the country's exports more expensive - and thus less competitive - at the same time as it makes money earned abroad worth less when it is repatriated. That cuts into the earnings of Japanese exporters as the nation struggles to sustain economic growth. \par \par \uc2  Tuesday's developments underscore the paradox facing Japan: long and painstaking efforts to bolster the economy have finally convinced many investors that Japan is a good buy; as a result, the yen has risen, potentially undermining the prospects for an economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  "The government thinks the yen's rise would have a bad impact on the economy, including exporters," said Hajime Sato, assistant general manager of the treasury department at Daiwa International Trust Bank. \par \par \uc2  Haruhiko Kuroda, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 's vice minister for international affairs, confirmed the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday, and warned that the MOF would continue to monitor \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves and take further "decisive steps" if necessary. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought between $2 billion and $3 billion in fairly thin trading, but analysts said that while the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  lent some support to the dollar, the tide continues to flow in the yen's favor. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  came in the wake of the dollar's fall to 101.36 yen in New York late Monday, approaching its 1999 low of 101.25 yen and below levels where the BOJ last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the yen's rise on Dec. 24. \par \par \uc2  Sentiment favoring the yen is widespread in Tokyo. A prominently displayed survey of 10 \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  analysts published Tuesday showed a unanimous view that the dollar will dip below 100 yen in the first half of 2000. Full-year estimates ranged between 85 yen and 125 yen, and all of them put the dollar's bottom at 95 yen or lower. \par \par \uc2  In addition to bullishness about Japan's economic outlook, a seeming lack of urgency on the BOJ's part could pave the way for further gains by the yen. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to leave key interest rates unchanged at its regular governing council meeting Wednesday. But ECB President Wim Duisenberg, who doesn't want to surprise markets with sudden shifts in policy, may well use the opportunity at a press conference after the meeting to prepare financial markets for a rate hike as soon as Feb. 3, observers say. \par \par \uc2  Against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  late Tuesday in New York, the dollar was quoted at 1.5660 Swiss francs, down slightly from 1.5648 Swiss francs late Monday in New York, and at 1.4523 Canadian dollars, up from C$1.4463 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  In Latin America, Mexico's peso ended sharply weaker against the dollar, hurt by losses in global stock markets. Mexico's IPC stock index tumbled more than 5% Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The Mexican peso was quoted at 9.5150 to the dollar, compared with 9.4120 pesos to the dollar at Monday's close. \par \par \uc2  The Brazilian real closed sharply weaker against the dollar Tuesday, with the market spooked by falls in Brazilian and international stock markets, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Brazil's Bovespa index tumbled 1079.42 points, or 6.4%, to close at 15851. \par \par \uc2  The real closed at 1.8520 to the dollar, compared with Monday's close of 1.8200 reals to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  late in the trading day when the real reached 1.8600 per dollar, selling dollars to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  brought the real back to 1.8490 per dollar, but was unable to reverse the day's sharp losses. \par \par \uc2  Copyright (c) 2000 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2  1034 1863 28038 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument djon000020020330dw1400tyf\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (japan near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/1995 bis 21/08/2023\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\